1
00:00:02,141 --> 00:00:04,210
[tense music]

2
00:00:55,928 --> 00:00:59,131
[engine revving]

3
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:11,444
[metal crashes]

4
00:01:21,654 --> 00:01:24,156
[indistinct chatter]

5
00:01:29,795 --> 00:01:33,198
[faint thumping]

6
00:01:37,035 --> 00:01:41,073
[man speaking indistinctly]

7
00:01:41,974 --> 00:01:43,642
[keys jingling]

8
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,481
[clicks]

9
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:58,524
[man over earpiece]
He's coming down.

10
00:01:59,825 --> 00:02:01,093
[telephone ringing]

11
00:02:01,193 --> 00:02:04,029
[gate opening]

12
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:08,200
[indistinct chatter]

13
00:02:13,939 --> 00:02:15,073
[elevator bell dings]

14
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:23,582
Well, I wanted to reassure
you and your father,

15
00:02:23,682 --> 00:02:24,717
you're in good hands.

16
00:02:25,851 --> 00:02:27,185
Ambitious...

17
00:02:27,286 --> 00:02:29,254
- How'd it go?
- Almost done.

18
00:02:29,355 --> 00:02:31,056
[businessman
speaks indistinctly]

19
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:42,735
All this...

20
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:45,704
began with that.

21
00:02:46,605 --> 00:02:49,107
We're gonna take great care
of your company, sir.

22
00:02:50,876 --> 00:02:51,977
I know you will.

23
00:02:55,147 --> 00:02:58,917
[businessman
speaks indistinctly]

24
00:02:59,918 --> 00:03:01,320
[car honks]

25
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:02,955
[businessman]
All right, gentlemen.

26
00:03:03,055 --> 00:03:04,957
See you in a week
when we make it official.

27
00:03:05,057 --> 00:03:06,559
Great day.

28
00:03:07,092 --> 00:03:08,260
[car door opens]

29
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:12,898
[car door closes]

30
00:03:14,166 --> 00:03:15,334
Congrats.

31
00:03:15,434 --> 00:03:16,502
Thank you, brother.

32
00:03:36,755 --> 00:03:38,691
Relax.

33
00:03:38,791 --> 00:03:41,226
This is what you wanted.
You should be happy.

34
00:03:41,326 --> 00:03:42,428
I am.

35
00:03:43,462 --> 00:03:44,530
Are you?

36
00:03:46,965 --> 00:03:48,467
For me, it's, uh...

37
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:50,836
bittersweet.

38
00:03:57,175 --> 00:04:00,045
[soft music]

39
00:04:24,302 --> 00:04:25,638
- [Tibu] Thank you.
- [staff speaks Thai]

40
00:04:33,546 --> 00:04:34,980
[Tibu in English] Do what
you need to do, then come over

41
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,749
so we can settle
our business, yeah?

42
00:04:36,849 --> 00:04:38,083
[Cole] Sure.

43
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:56,569
- [Cole] All good?
- Yeah, all good.

44
00:04:58,236 --> 00:05:00,473
Oh, and, boss, uh,
tomorrow night's guest list

45
00:05:00,573 --> 00:05:01,674
just came through.

46
00:05:01,774 --> 00:05:02,908
It's on your tablet.

47
00:05:03,008 --> 00:05:04,677
[Cole] Thanks. I'll take a look.

48
00:05:05,778 --> 00:05:06,845
[door opens]

49
00:05:13,519 --> 00:05:15,621
How did you become
so good at this?

50
00:05:17,122 --> 00:05:21,259
When I was a rookie,
they had me work the jail.

51
00:05:23,529 --> 00:05:26,599
Best chess players in the world
live behind bars.

52
00:05:27,533 --> 00:05:28,467
Mm.

53
00:05:30,536 --> 00:05:32,304
Do you miss
being a police officer?

54
00:05:33,038 --> 00:05:34,540
I miss the action.

55
00:05:35,941 --> 00:05:37,309
Not the politics.

56
00:05:37,409 --> 00:05:38,644
- [chess piece thuds]
- Check.

57
00:05:41,113 --> 00:05:42,548
[Tibu] You can never go back?

58
00:05:43,148 --> 00:05:44,617
[Cole] No.

59
00:05:44,717 --> 00:05:46,051
I made some mistakes.

60
00:05:47,085 --> 00:05:49,321
Pissed off the wrong people.

61
00:05:49,421 --> 00:05:50,489
[inhales sharply]

62
00:05:51,624 --> 00:05:53,125
Today, um...

63
00:05:55,127 --> 00:05:56,461
would have been
your father's birthday.

64
00:05:56,562 --> 00:05:57,830
[chuckles]

65
00:05:59,231 --> 00:06:01,033
Trying to break
my concentration.

66
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:02,501
Whatever it takes to win.

67
00:06:03,902 --> 00:06:05,638
Well, you'll need
all the help you can get.

68
00:06:05,738 --> 00:06:07,239
[chuckles]

69
00:06:12,945 --> 00:06:14,012
You're okay?

70
00:06:17,149 --> 00:06:18,116
Yeah.

71
00:06:20,485 --> 00:06:21,520
Thanks for remembering.

72
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:24,523
Oh. I wish I could have met him.

73
00:06:24,623 --> 00:06:26,024
[Cole] Yeah, you'd have
loved him.

74
00:06:27,192 --> 00:06:28,694
He was, uh...

75
00:06:31,864 --> 00:06:33,331
I mean, he could play.

76
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:36,001
He'd have kicked your ass
worse than I do.

77
00:06:36,101 --> 00:06:38,837
- [chuckles]
- And taken your money.

78
00:06:40,205 --> 00:06:41,607
Check.

79
00:06:41,707 --> 00:06:43,008
[exhales]

80
00:06:46,044 --> 00:06:48,947
If you were me,
what would you do?

81
00:06:50,315 --> 00:06:51,817
I'd probably surrender.

82
00:06:53,351 --> 00:06:54,419
Ahh.

83
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:56,822
[Tibu laughing]

84
00:06:57,856 --> 00:07:00,092
- But you don't have to.
- Ah.

85
00:07:00,192 --> 00:07:01,359
No, you've won.

86
00:07:01,459 --> 00:07:03,028
[both chuckle]

87
00:07:07,733 --> 00:07:09,635
[gulps, inhales]

88
00:07:09,735 --> 00:07:10,736
[smacks lips]

89
00:07:21,546 --> 00:07:22,581
[chuckles softly]

90
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:29,321
[sighs]

91
00:07:31,657 --> 00:07:33,926
[clears throat]

92
00:07:38,997 --> 00:07:40,432
Happy birthday, Dad.

93
00:07:47,072 --> 00:07:49,207
[birds chirping]

94
00:08:03,421 --> 00:08:04,857
[staff speaks Thai]

95
00:08:04,957 --> 00:08:05,958
[Kameron in English] The dinner
precedes cake cutting.

96
00:08:06,058 --> 00:08:06,992
Ready for your big night?

97
00:08:07,092 --> 00:08:08,426
My father's gonna make a speech.

98
00:08:08,526 --> 00:08:10,028
- You know how much I hate this.
- [both chuckle]

99
00:08:12,631 --> 00:08:13,832
[engine starts]

100
00:08:13,932 --> 00:08:15,100
[speaks Thai]

101
00:08:22,374 --> 00:08:24,677
[in English] Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
Yes, well, it was like, um,

102
00:08:24,777 --> 00:08:26,611
what is-- what is this language
you've been learning?

103
00:08:26,712 --> 00:08:28,346
I don't-- I don't recognize it.

104
00:08:28,446 --> 00:08:29,915
Are you sure
you've been learning?

105
00:08:30,949 --> 00:08:32,751
[muffled laughter]

106
00:08:33,585 --> 00:08:35,453
[speaking Thai]

107
00:08:35,553 --> 00:08:38,056
[all exclaim]

108
00:08:39,925 --> 00:08:41,894
[speaking Thai indistinctly]

109
00:08:44,129 --> 00:08:46,665
[chattering, laughing]

110
00:08:55,007 --> 00:08:56,842
[tapping glass]

111
00:08:58,010 --> 00:08:59,544
[in English] I have.
I have, yeah. I went last year.

112
00:08:59,644 --> 00:09:00,645
[Tibu clears throat]

113
00:09:00,746 --> 00:09:02,681
[breathes deeply]

114
00:09:02,781 --> 00:09:05,684
You spend your life
chasing success,

115
00:09:05,784 --> 00:09:08,721
only to one day realize
that all that matters

116
00:09:08,821 --> 00:09:10,823
is how you achieved it.

117
00:09:10,923 --> 00:09:12,324
What you've left behind.

118
00:09:13,692 --> 00:09:16,394
- Ours is a very dirty business.
- Who's that?

119
00:09:16,494 --> 00:09:19,732
[Tibu] But our company's
"ethics over profits" spirit...

120
00:09:19,832 --> 00:09:22,567
[Taran] Jaran Daniles.
Trans-Pacific Exports.

121
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:26,504
Cleanest record on the high seas
over the past 40 years,

122
00:09:26,604 --> 00:09:29,775
and that... is what
I am most proud of.

123
00:09:29,875 --> 00:09:32,110
- [guest 1] Yes.
- [guests clapping]

124
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:33,545
[guest 2] Bravo.

125
00:09:36,882 --> 00:09:38,516
[Tibu] I'd like to thank you
for joining me...

126
00:09:38,616 --> 00:09:39,952
- [man] Yes. Good to meet you.
- ...and my son Kameron

127
00:09:40,052 --> 00:09:41,787
on this special occasion.

128
00:09:41,887 --> 00:09:43,388
[man] El Salvador.

129
00:09:43,488 --> 00:09:45,257
[Tibu] Tonight, we celebrate
a new chapter

130
00:09:45,357 --> 00:09:47,092
for the Campallo family.

131
00:09:47,192 --> 00:09:48,526
A new beginning.

132
00:09:49,494 --> 00:09:51,296
I'm so proud
of the work Kameron did

133
00:09:51,396 --> 00:09:52,697
to grow the business,

134
00:09:52,798 --> 00:09:55,533
to help make this sale
a reality.

135
00:09:55,633 --> 00:09:56,601
Without his efforts,
none of this

136
00:09:56,701 --> 00:09:58,403
would have been possible.

137
00:09:58,503 --> 00:10:00,538
And we did it the right way.

138
00:10:02,074 --> 00:10:03,041
Together.

139
00:10:04,509 --> 00:10:05,911
Come.

140
00:10:06,011 --> 00:10:08,046
[guests clapping and cheering]

141
00:10:13,151 --> 00:10:15,353
[guests cheering loudly]

142
00:10:23,528 --> 00:10:25,330
Now, we toast and drink.

143
00:10:25,764 --> 00:10:28,266
[cheering continues]

144
00:10:30,535 --> 00:10:32,037
[Tibu] To celebrate this day.

145
00:10:36,775 --> 00:10:38,276
The one you wanted.

146
00:10:39,511 --> 00:10:40,946
Thank you.

147
00:10:41,046 --> 00:10:42,280
- Thank you.
- [guests clapping]

148
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:44,016
Cole, where are you?

149
00:10:45,884 --> 00:10:47,853
Come. Join the family.

150
00:10:56,261 --> 00:10:57,395
Open it.

151
00:11:01,099 --> 00:11:02,467
Kameron likes the flash,

152
00:11:02,567 --> 00:11:03,969
but, uh, we prefer this, right?

153
00:11:04,069 --> 00:11:06,939
This is a watch
for a man of action. [chuckles]

154
00:11:07,973 --> 00:11:09,541
- Uh, read the back.
- [box thuds]

155
00:11:12,610 --> 00:11:14,079
What does the inscription say?

156
00:11:14,913 --> 00:11:16,048
It's a date.

157
00:11:17,082 --> 00:11:19,117
It's the day he saved my life.

158
00:11:19,217 --> 00:11:23,155
Five years ago,
he risked his life to save mine.

159
00:11:23,255 --> 00:11:24,789
I offered him a job,

160
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:27,525
and he has since become family.

161
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:29,761
[guests clapping]

162
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:33,198
Thanks, Tibu.

163
00:11:33,298 --> 00:11:35,400
[Tibu] Thank you. Thank you.

164
00:11:38,003 --> 00:11:40,505
- To family.
- [guests] To family!

165
00:11:40,605 --> 00:11:43,008
[cheering]

166
00:11:44,076 --> 00:11:45,377
They're celebrating.

167
00:11:45,477 --> 00:11:46,578
But don't worry.

168
00:11:47,779 --> 00:11:49,514
The sale will be dead tonight.

169
00:11:56,454 --> 00:11:58,156
Wasn't so bad, now, was it?

170
00:11:58,256 --> 00:11:59,824
[chuckles]

171
00:11:59,925 --> 00:12:01,259
It was a wonderful night.

172
00:12:04,162 --> 00:12:05,463
Everything okay?

173
00:12:06,331 --> 00:12:07,432
Yeah.

174
00:12:08,867 --> 00:12:12,504
I just, uh, never imagined
I would ever sell the company.

175
00:12:13,505 --> 00:12:14,672
Never wanted to.

176
00:12:17,475 --> 00:12:18,710
Then why'd you do it?

177
00:12:25,817 --> 00:12:27,185
I did it for Kameron.

178
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,787
KMG was, uh...

179
00:12:31,056 --> 00:12:32,590
my dream, not his.

180
00:12:33,291 --> 00:12:36,461
The shipping business
is, uh, not for him.

181
00:12:39,231 --> 00:12:42,000
I wanted to give him the chance
to chase his own dreams.

182
00:12:44,869 --> 00:12:46,571
He'll never forget it, Tibu.

183
00:12:49,874 --> 00:12:50,976
Thank you.

184
00:12:54,046 --> 00:12:55,480
Why are we going this way?

185
00:12:58,483 --> 00:13:00,652
Looks like a road closure.

186
00:13:17,102 --> 00:13:18,303
[policeman 1 speaks Thai]

187
00:13:18,403 --> 00:13:20,338
[policeman 2 speaking Thai]

188
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:26,644
[in English] I'll back us
out of here.

189
00:13:26,744 --> 00:13:30,182
[policeman 1 speaking Thai]

190
00:13:32,684 --> 00:13:34,186
- [brake squeals]
- [policeman 2 speaking Thai]

191
00:13:36,554 --> 00:13:37,622
[exclaims in Thai]

192
00:13:37,722 --> 00:13:38,690
[in English] What is this?

193
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:39,891
[policeman 1 speaks Thai]

194
00:13:41,559 --> 00:13:43,161
[policeman 2 speaking Thai]

195
00:13:43,261 --> 00:13:44,296
[exclaims in Thai]

196
00:13:53,705 --> 00:13:54,772
- [in English] Get down!
- [gunshots]

197
00:13:54,872 --> 00:13:56,441
[yelps]

198
00:13:56,541 --> 00:13:57,909
[hitman] Take 'em down!

199
00:14:00,945 --> 00:14:02,147
[engine revving]

200
00:14:05,383 --> 00:14:06,884
- [gunshots]
- [tires screech]

201
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,955
- [grunts]
- [car alarm wailing]

202
00:14:11,656 --> 00:14:12,657
Ahh!

203
00:14:14,292 --> 00:14:15,994
- [gunshots]
- [hitman] Shoot the tires!

204
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:19,964
- [car engine whirring]
- You okay?

205
00:14:20,065 --> 00:14:21,433
I'm okay.

206
00:14:27,272 --> 00:14:31,043
- [engine revving]
- [tires screeching]

207
00:14:31,143 --> 00:14:34,179
- [gunman yelling in pain]
- Ah!

208
00:14:36,081 --> 00:14:39,117
[Tibu breathing shakily]

209
00:14:41,986 --> 00:14:44,122
- [Cole] Ah, shit.
- [distant police siren wailing]

210
00:14:45,023 --> 00:14:47,159
[Tibu] What just happened?

211
00:14:47,259 --> 00:14:48,693
[shakily] Those were police.

212
00:14:51,763 --> 00:14:54,232
[shallow breathing]

213
00:14:54,332 --> 00:14:56,068
- Please...
- [Cole sighs]

214
00:14:56,168 --> 00:14:58,070
Please look after Kameron.

215
00:14:58,603 --> 00:15:01,739
[labored breathing] Look at me.

216
00:15:01,839 --> 00:15:04,109
If-- if I don't make it,
I can't help him.

217
00:15:04,209 --> 00:15:06,378
Nothing will happen to Kameron.

218
00:15:06,978 --> 00:15:09,247
- [gasping rapidly]
- Stay with me, Tibu.

219
00:15:09,347 --> 00:15:10,515
Stay with me.

220
00:15:10,615 --> 00:15:12,917
[continues gasping rapidly]

221
00:15:13,017 --> 00:15:13,985
[gasping stops]

222
00:15:18,056 --> 00:15:20,958
[emotional music]

223
00:15:35,073 --> 00:15:36,508
[cell phone rings]

224
00:15:38,042 --> 00:15:38,976
Yeah?

225
00:15:39,077 --> 00:15:40,245
[Cole over phone]
Taran,

226
00:15:40,345 --> 00:15:41,779
is Kameron with you?

227
00:15:42,247 --> 00:15:44,749
[Taran] Yeah. I've got eyes
on him. He's just got back.

228
00:15:44,849 --> 00:15:47,619
Listen, we were ambushed.

229
00:15:47,719 --> 00:15:49,020
Tibu's dead.

230
00:15:50,522 --> 00:15:51,589
The fuck?

231
00:15:53,725 --> 00:15:54,992
Did you call the police?

232
00:15:55,093 --> 00:15:56,761
The police are involved.

233
00:15:56,861 --> 00:15:58,530
We can't trust anybody.

234
00:16:01,433 --> 00:16:02,934
[zipper unzips]

235
00:16:05,337 --> 00:16:07,105
One of these guys was American.

236
00:16:07,205 --> 00:16:08,673
US passport.

237
00:16:08,773 --> 00:16:11,276
-
6573247. Run it.
- [cell phone thuds]

238
00:16:12,444 --> 00:16:14,346
3247.

239
00:16:14,446 --> 00:16:15,747
Checking. Stand by.

240
00:16:16,848 --> 00:16:19,117
I've got him. Jonathan Rogers.

241
00:16:19,217 --> 00:16:21,052
Former marine. MARSOC.

242
00:16:22,387 --> 00:16:24,356
Rogers is a crewman for the KMG.

243
00:16:25,022 --> 00:16:26,658
He works for us.

244
00:16:26,758 --> 00:16:28,926
He's departing
on the Artemis tonight.

245
00:16:29,026 --> 00:16:30,695
It's gonna leave port
in two hours.

246
00:16:31,729 --> 00:16:32,864
What's your plan?

247
00:16:33,798 --> 00:16:35,200
[Cole] I'm headed to the port.

248
00:16:36,468 --> 00:16:37,935
I'll find out who did this.

249
00:16:41,473 --> 00:16:43,641
[indistinct chattering
on tablet]

250
00:16:44,942 --> 00:16:46,544
Campallo is dead, sir.

251
00:16:47,745 --> 00:16:48,780
Good.

252
00:16:50,882 --> 00:16:53,451
So, what do you want?

253
00:16:53,551 --> 00:16:54,919
We have a problem, sir.

254
00:16:56,221 --> 00:16:57,589
His bodyguard got away.

255
00:17:04,896 --> 00:17:06,798
Tell the police
to put out an APB.

256
00:17:08,266 --> 00:17:10,302
But... one more thing.

257
00:17:12,237 --> 00:17:13,938
Don't bring him in alive.

258
00:17:19,811 --> 00:17:21,746
[reporter on TV]
Two police
officers were murdered tonight

259
00:17:21,846 --> 00:17:24,382
while performing
a routine traffic stop.

260
00:17:24,482 --> 00:17:27,885
Billionaire shipping tycoon
Manuel Tibu Campallo

261
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:29,921
-
was also killed.
- [gift wrapper rustles]

262
00:17:30,021 --> 00:17:32,224
The suspect
is a British citizen

263
00:17:32,324 --> 00:17:33,725
named Cole Reed.

264
00:17:33,825 --> 00:17:36,994
Reed worked as
Campallo's personal bodyguard.

265
00:17:37,962 --> 00:17:41,733
The suspect is very dangerous
and still on the loose.

266
00:17:41,833 --> 00:17:44,736
A citywide order to shelter
is in place until--

267
00:17:44,836 --> 00:17:46,538
[buzzing]

268
00:17:46,638 --> 00:17:50,942
[continues buzzing]

269
00:17:51,042 --> 00:17:52,577
- This is Ellis.
- [man over phone]
Miss Ellis,

270
00:17:52,677 --> 00:17:54,212
we need you
to report immediately.

271
00:17:54,846 --> 00:17:57,349
- Well, I, um--
-
The Artemis is short crew.

272
00:17:57,449 --> 00:17:58,850
Departs at midnight.

273
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:00,084
We need you there now.

274
00:18:00,985 --> 00:18:03,555
Sir, I just got in
from the Venus San Diego haul,

275
00:18:03,655 --> 00:18:06,924
24 days across, and my flight,
well, it's in, uh,

276
00:18:07,024 --> 00:18:08,125
my flight home's in three hours.

277
00:18:08,226 --> 00:18:09,227
Miss Ellis, you're still

278
00:18:09,327 --> 00:18:11,128
a probationary employee.

279
00:18:11,229 --> 00:18:14,332
Sir, I-I have my daughter
this weekend in LA.

280
00:18:14,432 --> 00:18:16,568
Listen, if you're not
at your post

281
00:18:16,668 --> 00:18:18,370
on the Artemis in an hour,

282
00:18:18,470 --> 00:18:20,238
KMG's gonna have to let you go.

283
00:18:20,338 --> 00:18:21,506
[scoffs]

284
00:18:22,139 --> 00:18:24,242
Okay. Roger that.

285
00:18:25,877 --> 00:18:26,911
Fuck.

286
00:18:27,512 --> 00:18:28,546
Fuck.

287
00:18:29,714 --> 00:18:31,082
[exhales] Oh, fuck.

288
00:18:41,025 --> 00:18:42,594
[Cole exhales sharply]

289
00:18:59,210 --> 00:19:01,779
[keypad beeping]

290
00:19:01,879 --> 00:19:04,916
[beeping continues]

291
00:19:06,551 --> 00:19:09,587
[door opens, closes]

292
00:19:11,856 --> 00:19:14,191
Kameron,
Detective Jamai is here.

293
00:19:15,893 --> 00:19:17,362
- [Kameron] Evening, Detective.
- Good evening.

294
00:19:17,462 --> 00:19:18,796
[Kameron] Evening, Officer.

295
00:19:18,896 --> 00:19:19,864
My condolences.

296
00:19:19,964 --> 00:19:20,965
Thank you.

297
00:19:21,065 --> 00:19:22,834
I am sorry, but we are going

298
00:19:22,934 --> 00:19:24,536
to have to ask you
a few questions.

299
00:19:24,636 --> 00:19:26,704
- [sniffles] Of course. Ah...
- [phone buzzes]

300
00:19:26,804 --> 00:19:28,205
[continues buzzing]

301
00:19:28,306 --> 00:19:29,674
Uh, Taran, could you pour
these gentlemen

302
00:19:29,774 --> 00:19:31,208
- a drink, please?
- Of course.

303
00:19:31,309 --> 00:19:33,345
Hello? Who is this?

304
00:19:33,445 --> 00:19:34,912
[over phone]
Kameron, it's Cole.

305
00:19:36,714 --> 00:19:37,649
Listen.

306
00:19:39,551 --> 00:19:40,818
Your father, uh...

307
00:19:43,721 --> 00:19:44,656
[inhales]

308
00:19:46,123 --> 00:19:47,325
I'm so sorry.

309
00:19:48,259 --> 00:19:49,594
[sighs] I tried.

310
00:19:51,128 --> 00:19:53,398
The police are here
asking questions.

311
00:19:53,498 --> 00:19:55,232
On the news,
they're saying you killed him.

312
00:19:55,333 --> 00:19:56,801
That's not what happened.

313
00:19:58,336 --> 00:19:59,471
We were ambushed.

314
00:20:00,505 --> 00:20:01,906
You need to stay locked down.

315
00:20:02,774 --> 00:20:05,743
Whoever killed Tibu
will be coming for you next.

316
00:20:11,282 --> 00:20:12,484
[exhales, sniffles]

317
00:20:12,584 --> 00:20:14,786
[police siren wails in distance]

318
00:20:22,159 --> 00:20:23,260
[phone thuds]

319
00:20:31,135 --> 00:20:32,537
[port guard 1 speaking Thai]

320
00:20:32,637 --> 00:20:35,106
[indistinct announcement
over PA]

321
00:20:42,346 --> 00:20:43,615
[siren wails]

322
00:20:45,950 --> 00:20:48,820
[speaking Thai over radio]

323
00:20:52,356 --> 00:20:56,193
[port security speaking in Thai]

324
00:20:57,294 --> 00:20:59,831
[tense music]

325
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,637
[port guard 2 speaking Thai]

326
00:21:10,975 --> 00:21:12,376
[keyboard clacks]

327
00:21:13,511 --> 00:21:15,046
[port guard 1 in English]
Make your way through security

328
00:21:15,146 --> 00:21:16,247
on your right.

329
00:21:18,583 --> 00:21:21,753
[port worker 1 speaks Thai]

330
00:21:30,562 --> 00:21:34,632
[indistinct chatter]

331
00:21:35,232 --> 00:21:36,768
[port worker 2 speaks Thai]

332
00:21:59,924 --> 00:22:00,958
[device beeps]

333
00:22:01,759 --> 00:22:02,727
[port worker 3 speaks Thai]

334
00:22:07,131 --> 00:22:08,666
[port worker 2 speaks Thai]

335
00:22:09,266 --> 00:22:12,303
[port worker talks indistinctly]

336
00:22:17,542 --> 00:22:18,810
[crewman in English]
Hey, Jonathan!

337
00:22:24,048 --> 00:22:26,484
[tense music continues]

338
00:22:29,887 --> 00:22:31,823
[keypad beeping]

339
00:22:31,923 --> 00:22:33,925
[news alert tune plays]

340
00:22:34,025 --> 00:22:35,693
[reporter on TV]
For more
on this developing story,

341
00:22:35,793 --> 00:22:38,195
we go live to Stan Beckwith
on the scene.

342
00:22:38,295 --> 00:22:40,131
[Stan]
New details
are emerging tonight

343
00:22:40,231 --> 00:22:42,534
following a shooting
in downtown Bangkok.

344
00:22:42,634 --> 00:22:44,068
Sources say
the incident may have been

345
00:22:44,168 --> 00:22:45,336
an attempted kidnapping

346
00:22:45,436 --> 00:22:47,071
targeting KMG CEO

347
00:22:47,171 --> 00:22:49,073
Manuel Tibu Campallo,

348
00:22:49,173 --> 00:22:51,408
allegedly carried out
by his longtime bodyguard,

349
00:22:51,509 --> 00:22:52,710
Cole Reed.

350
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:54,178
Campallo was pronounced dead

351
00:22:54,278 --> 00:22:55,346
at the scene.

352
00:22:55,446 --> 00:22:56,413
Captain. [knocks]

353
00:22:57,982 --> 00:22:59,083
You may enter.

354
00:23:00,151 --> 00:23:03,555
- Is everybody on board?
- Yes, sir. We're good.

355
00:23:04,255 --> 00:23:06,090
Who are you, and what are you
doing on my bridge?

356
00:23:06,190 --> 00:23:07,925
[Mateo] New third mate, Captain.

357
00:23:08,025 --> 00:23:09,026
I don't need a third mate.

358
00:23:09,126 --> 00:23:10,995
I have 20 good men on board.

359
00:23:11,095 --> 00:23:12,597
Well, Captain,
I didn't wanna be here either,

360
00:23:12,697 --> 00:23:14,899
but, uh, company asked me
to report.

361
00:23:14,999 --> 00:23:16,067
Rama called in sick, sir.

362
00:23:16,167 --> 00:23:17,468
KMG sent her.

363
00:23:19,871 --> 00:23:21,138
[exhales sharply]

364
00:23:23,775 --> 00:23:26,878
[smacks lips]
Would you like me to twirl, sir?

365
00:23:29,547 --> 00:23:31,048
I'm not a fan of attitude.

366
00:23:31,148 --> 00:23:33,384
Oh, no, neither am I. At all.

367
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:38,556
[paper rustles softly]

368
00:23:41,025 --> 00:23:44,128
Well, if the company,
in all its genius,

369
00:23:44,228 --> 00:23:46,631
wants you here,
then welcome on board.

370
00:23:47,531 --> 00:23:48,966
[Angie] I like
your necklace, sir.

371
00:23:52,003 --> 00:23:53,605
- You know what it is?
- I do.

372
00:23:53,705 --> 00:23:56,540
That is a Viking symbol
of guidance and protection.

373
00:24:00,044 --> 00:24:01,879
Impressive. Theo.

374
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:04,315
Can you take the young lady
to her cabin?

375
00:24:04,415 --> 00:24:05,482
[Theo] Sir.

376
00:24:06,350 --> 00:24:07,384
[Angie] Thank you.

377
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:10,254
You're welcome.

378
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:17,294
Anything else, sir?

379
00:24:17,829 --> 00:24:20,497
[Marko sighs] The two of you
are on the night shift.

380
00:24:20,598 --> 00:24:21,833
Keep an eye on her.

381
00:24:29,106 --> 00:24:31,776
[tense music]

382
00:25:08,412 --> 00:25:10,748
[horn blaring]

383
00:25:14,485 --> 00:25:16,888
- Hard to starboard!
- [Theo] Hard to starboard.

384
00:25:18,723 --> 00:25:20,557
Hard to starboard now.

385
00:25:29,801 --> 00:25:32,670
[dramatic music]

386
00:25:42,146 --> 00:25:43,247
[exhales]

387
00:26:24,822 --> 00:26:26,390
- [knock on door]
- Yeah?

388
00:26:26,490 --> 00:26:28,659
[Mateo] Captain has us
on night shift.

389
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:30,461
All right, I'll be there
in a sec.

390
00:26:35,066 --> 00:26:37,334
[dramatic music continues]

391
00:27:13,504 --> 00:27:15,406
[radio feedback squeals,
static crackles]

392
00:27:24,916 --> 00:27:27,251
[muffled sobbing]

393
00:27:27,351 --> 00:27:30,121
[muffled thudding]

394
00:27:30,221 --> 00:27:32,056
[woman speaks indistinctly]

395
00:27:37,061 --> 00:27:39,430
[lever handle creaking, thuds]

396
00:27:40,898 --> 00:27:43,434
[metal groaning]

397
00:27:49,206 --> 00:27:52,643
[faint thumping]

398
00:27:57,214 --> 00:28:00,151
[thumping continues]

399
00:28:04,155 --> 00:28:08,059
[metal groaning]

400
00:28:18,970 --> 00:28:20,804
[woman speaks indistinctly]

401
00:28:27,011 --> 00:28:29,914
[muffled thudding]

402
00:28:30,014 --> 00:28:31,415
[woman speaks indistinctly]

403
00:28:31,515 --> 00:28:33,417
[muffled thudding]

404
00:28:39,423 --> 00:28:42,326
[metal groaning]

405
00:28:44,495 --> 00:28:47,531
[suspenseful music]

406
00:28:53,770 --> 00:28:57,641
[muffled sobbing]

407
00:29:02,446 --> 00:29:03,647
[woman speaks indistinctly]

408
00:29:07,151 --> 00:29:08,852
[muffled cry]

409
00:29:08,953 --> 00:29:09,987
[flashlight clicks]

410
00:29:11,722 --> 00:29:13,490
[Cole exhales sharply]

411
00:29:15,392 --> 00:29:16,360
[flashlight clicks]

412
00:29:18,362 --> 00:29:20,764
[clattering]

413
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:22,066
[clunks]

414
00:29:29,974 --> 00:29:31,742
[clunks]

415
00:29:34,711 --> 00:29:36,680
- [thud]
- [door squeaks]

416
00:29:39,483 --> 00:29:42,386
[all gasp, whimper]

417
00:29:51,262 --> 00:29:53,464
- [woman mumbles]
- [Cole] It's okay.

418
00:29:53,564 --> 00:29:55,866
It's okay. I'm here to help.

419
00:29:57,701 --> 00:29:59,003
How did you get here?

420
00:29:59,103 --> 00:30:00,837
Does anyone speak English?

421
00:30:00,938 --> 00:30:03,074
Doctor. Doctor.

422
00:30:03,174 --> 00:30:04,441
Doctor.

423
00:30:07,044 --> 00:30:08,579
You speak English?

424
00:30:08,679 --> 00:30:10,647
[man coughs]

425
00:30:10,747 --> 00:30:12,383
How long have you been in here?

426
00:30:13,084 --> 00:30:14,118
Bangkok.

427
00:30:14,218 --> 00:30:15,452
They say they let us out

428
00:30:15,552 --> 00:30:17,254
as soon as leave port,

429
00:30:17,354 --> 00:30:19,490
but they leave us in dark.

430
00:30:19,590 --> 00:30:21,825
- Hot, dark.
- [Cole] Wait, wait.

431
00:30:21,925 --> 00:30:23,860
Please. Sit down.

432
00:30:24,795 --> 00:30:26,163
We need to be quiet.

433
00:30:26,263 --> 00:30:29,700
[speaks Thai]

434
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:31,435
[Cole in English]
I'm gonna help you.

435
00:30:31,902 --> 00:30:33,237
I'm gonna bring you water...

436
00:30:34,205 --> 00:30:35,606
and food.

437
00:30:35,706 --> 00:30:37,541
Some medical supplies.

438
00:30:37,641 --> 00:30:38,642
[Seng breathes shakily]

439
00:30:38,742 --> 00:30:42,013
[translating in Thai]

440
00:30:42,113 --> 00:30:43,380
[Angie in English] Hello?

441
00:30:45,816 --> 00:30:47,384
[Cole whispering]
You need to trust me.

442
00:30:47,484 --> 00:30:50,654
I'm coming back. For everybody.

443
00:30:50,754 --> 00:30:51,788
Okay?

444
00:30:53,590 --> 00:30:55,059
[lever handle thuds]

445
00:30:55,159 --> 00:30:56,160
[Angie] Hello?

446
00:30:56,260 --> 00:30:59,463
[metal groaning]

447
00:31:07,071 --> 00:31:08,505
Hello?

448
00:31:09,940 --> 00:31:11,408
Is anybody down here?

449
00:31:29,660 --> 00:31:32,063
- [thud]
- [door squeaking]

450
00:31:32,163 --> 00:31:34,331
- [Angie] Oh, my God.
- [all gasp]

451
00:31:34,431 --> 00:31:36,367
Oh, my God. [sniffles]

452
00:31:36,467 --> 00:31:39,370
Okay. It's-it's-- it's okay.
C-come.

453
00:31:39,470 --> 00:31:40,771
Come. One by one.

454
00:31:42,273 --> 00:31:45,176
All right, just-just--
just stay in this area, okay?

455
00:31:45,276 --> 00:31:46,377
We'll help you.

456
00:31:47,178 --> 00:31:48,879
Okay. [breathes sharply]

457
00:31:48,979 --> 00:31:51,182
- Mateo?
- [radio static crackles]

458
00:31:51,982 --> 00:31:53,050
Fuck.

459
00:31:54,051 --> 00:31:56,753
Oh, God.
Your daughter's injured.

460
00:31:56,853 --> 00:31:58,722
Okay, is-is--
is anybody else injured?

461
00:31:59,756 --> 00:32:02,126
[Seng speaks Thai]

462
00:32:02,226 --> 00:32:03,560
[woman coughs]

463
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:04,961
[in English]
Uh, you with the man?

464
00:32:05,062 --> 00:32:07,898
Uh, he get us food and water

465
00:32:07,998 --> 00:32:09,400
a-and medicine for my daughter.

466
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:12,369
[Angie] What? W-what man? No.

467
00:32:12,469 --> 00:32:15,472
Look, just... stay calm.
We're gonna help you, all right?

468
00:32:15,572 --> 00:32:17,841
We're gonna get you food and
water. Just-- just stay calm.

469
00:32:18,675 --> 00:32:20,311
Josef!

470
00:32:20,411 --> 00:32:21,812
What's happening?

471
00:32:21,912 --> 00:32:23,447
These people need water
and a medic, all right?

472
00:32:23,547 --> 00:32:24,948
I'm gonna wake the captain.
Go help them.

473
00:32:25,682 --> 00:32:28,285
- Come on, go!
- Yes, I'll-- I'll handle it.

474
00:32:28,385 --> 00:32:31,322
[men whispering]

475
00:32:34,558 --> 00:32:36,693
[knocking on door]

476
00:32:37,828 --> 00:32:39,330
- [water splashes]
- [razor clangs]

477
00:32:39,430 --> 00:32:42,499
[Angie continues knocking]
Captain. Captain!

478
00:32:42,599 --> 00:32:44,135
- [water splashes]
- [razor clangs]

479
00:32:44,235 --> 00:32:45,602
[Angie knocks] Captain?

480
00:32:45,702 --> 00:32:46,770
Hold on.

481
00:32:50,006 --> 00:32:51,074
[towel thumps]

482
00:32:51,542 --> 00:32:52,776
- What is it?
- Captain,

483
00:32:52,876 --> 00:32:54,145
we found
a few dozen people locked

484
00:32:54,245 --> 00:32:55,279
in a container
in the lower hold.

485
00:32:55,379 --> 00:32:57,648
What? Come on in. Come on in.

486
00:32:57,748 --> 00:32:59,816
- They're not in good shape.
- What?

487
00:32:59,916 --> 00:33:02,319
- What-- what's going on?
- They're dehydrated. They're--

488
00:33:02,419 --> 00:33:04,255
[sighs]
Fuck, there's a little girl.

489
00:33:04,355 --> 00:33:05,789
Jesus Christ.

490
00:33:05,889 --> 00:33:07,191
Simon and Josef,
they're down there with them.

491
00:33:07,291 --> 00:33:08,625
- That's good. That's very good.
- Yeah.

492
00:33:08,725 --> 00:33:10,794
Now, calm down
and relax a little bit.

493
00:33:10,894 --> 00:33:12,263
- I'm calm.
- Have a seat.

494
00:33:15,132 --> 00:33:16,633
Captain to bridge.

495
00:33:16,733 --> 00:33:18,302
[Mateo over radio]
Go ahead, sir.

496
00:33:18,402 --> 00:33:19,770
Ellis found some people locked

497
00:33:19,870 --> 00:33:22,173
in one of the lower
container holds.

498
00:33:22,273 --> 00:33:23,607
She's here with me now.

499
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:25,842
Let's follow protocol.

500
00:33:25,942 --> 00:33:27,077
Yes, sir.

501
00:33:28,945 --> 00:33:29,913
[radio thuds]

502
00:33:30,647 --> 00:33:32,816
- We should call the navy, sir.
- Yes, I will.

503
00:33:32,916 --> 00:33:35,051
But let's find out
what's going on first.

504
00:33:35,152 --> 00:33:37,053
I think it's pretty clear
what's going on, sir.

505
00:33:37,154 --> 00:33:39,156
I hear you, and we got this.

506
00:33:39,256 --> 00:33:40,557
I'm gonna get a hold
of the doctor

507
00:33:40,657 --> 00:33:41,992
and you can guide him down,
okay?

508
00:33:42,092 --> 00:33:43,227
-
Jones for Captain.
- Sit down and relax.

509
00:33:43,327 --> 00:33:44,528
You did a good job.

510
00:33:44,628 --> 00:33:46,263
Very good. Please sit down.

511
00:33:47,464 --> 00:33:48,432
Sure.

512
00:33:49,500 --> 00:33:51,001
Marko. Come in.

513
00:33:51,101 --> 00:33:52,669
Do you need assistance, sir?

514
00:33:53,337 --> 00:33:55,206
No. Ellis is with me.

515
00:33:55,972 --> 00:33:58,509
And Mateo is-- is handling
protocol below.

516
00:33:59,843 --> 00:34:02,145
Maintain your position, please.
Thank you.

517
00:34:02,246 --> 00:34:03,580
Roger that, sir.

518
00:34:07,651 --> 00:34:10,254
[Josef] Everyone, get back
in the container. Let's go.

519
00:34:10,354 --> 00:34:11,522
[migrants speaking Thai]

520
00:34:11,622 --> 00:34:13,524
[Josef in English]
All of you, move.

521
00:34:13,624 --> 00:34:15,492
Get the fuck back inside.

522
00:34:15,592 --> 00:34:16,527
Now!

523
00:34:17,461 --> 00:34:19,162
[migrants yelping]

524
00:34:19,263 --> 00:34:21,398
- I said, get back in.
- [Simon] Get back!

525
00:34:21,498 --> 00:34:23,066
- [Josef] I said, get back in!
- [migrants screaming]

526
00:34:23,166 --> 00:34:25,001
Get back in the container!

527
00:34:25,702 --> 00:34:27,771
- Get back!
- [woman yelping]

528
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:31,074
[migrants continue screaming]

529
00:34:31,174 --> 00:34:32,709
I said, get back in!

530
00:34:33,944 --> 00:34:35,279
[Seng gasps]

531
00:34:36,713 --> 00:34:39,049
[Josef grunting]

532
00:34:41,017 --> 00:34:42,886
- You!
- [speaks Thai]

533
00:34:42,986 --> 00:34:44,455
[grunting]

534
00:34:44,555 --> 00:34:47,324
Aah! [yelling in pain]

535
00:34:48,492 --> 00:34:50,861
[grunting]

536
00:34:50,961 --> 00:34:51,962
[gunshots]

537
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:57,468
[grunts]

538
00:35:03,139 --> 00:35:04,941
[grunts, whimpers]

539
00:35:05,642 --> 00:35:06,910
[in English] Hey,
something's not right.

540
00:35:07,010 --> 00:35:08,445
We need to call the navy.

541
00:35:08,545 --> 00:35:09,813
- The captain just isn't--
- [gun cocks]

542
00:35:10,514 --> 00:35:11,982
[Mateo] We're not calling
anybody.

543
00:35:13,016 --> 00:35:13,984
[radio beeps]

544
00:35:15,051 --> 00:35:16,152
Mateo to Captain.

545
00:35:17,321 --> 00:35:18,455
Go for Captain.

546
00:35:18,555 --> 00:35:19,590
Got her on the bridge.

547
00:35:20,591 --> 00:35:21,858
I'm on my way.

548
00:35:23,394 --> 00:35:24,361
[knife rasps]

549
00:35:25,562 --> 00:35:28,665
- [yells]
- [both grunting]

550
00:35:28,765 --> 00:35:32,168
- [Josef groans in pain]
- [both grunting]

551
00:35:32,269 --> 00:35:33,570
[grunts]

552
00:35:35,572 --> 00:35:38,742
[both grunting]

553
00:35:39,276 --> 00:35:40,677
Step back.

554
00:35:40,777 --> 00:35:42,579
- Sit the fuck down.
- Okay.

555
00:35:42,679 --> 00:35:43,914
- [radio static crackles]
- [Angie grunts]

556
00:35:44,014 --> 00:35:46,417
- [gun clatters]
- [both grunting]

557
00:35:51,688 --> 00:35:55,258
[both grunting]

558
00:35:55,359 --> 00:35:57,093
[Josef straining]

559
00:35:57,193 --> 00:35:59,596
- Aah! [grunts]
- [Cole grunts]

560
00:35:59,696 --> 00:36:01,565
[screaming in pain]

561
00:36:03,700 --> 00:36:06,437
[yells, grunts in pain]

562
00:36:06,537 --> 00:36:07,771
[migrants screaming]

563
00:36:07,871 --> 00:36:09,673
[Dara speaks Thai]

564
00:36:09,773 --> 00:36:10,807
[gunshots]

565
00:36:12,976 --> 00:36:13,944
[Simon] Aah!

566
00:36:22,919 --> 00:36:24,154
[in English] We need to get you
off of this ship

567
00:36:24,254 --> 00:36:25,722
before the rest of them
get here.

568
00:36:26,289 --> 00:36:28,291
We need to go up
to the lifeboats.

569
00:36:28,392 --> 00:36:30,527
Stay close. Stay behind me.

570
00:36:30,627 --> 00:36:31,762
Let's move.

571
00:36:32,829 --> 00:36:35,432
[migrants conversing in Thai]

572
00:36:38,735 --> 00:36:40,771
[tense music]

573
00:36:41,972 --> 00:36:42,973
Fuck.

574
00:36:43,073 --> 00:36:44,074
[beeps]

575
00:36:44,174 --> 00:36:46,477
[signal beeping]

576
00:37:06,763 --> 00:37:07,764
[Angie] Aah!

577
00:37:08,965 --> 00:37:09,933
[Angie grunts]

578
00:37:10,467 --> 00:37:11,535
Come on.

579
00:37:14,938 --> 00:37:16,407
- Go fucking get her. Now.
- [crewman] Yes, sir.

580
00:37:16,507 --> 00:37:17,741
- Move!
- [Mateo groaning]

581
00:37:17,841 --> 00:37:20,276
What the fuck are you doing?
Get up!

582
00:37:20,377 --> 00:37:22,946
What the fuck's wrong
with you, huh?

583
00:37:23,046 --> 00:37:24,314
[Mateo]
It's still transmitting, sir.

584
00:37:24,415 --> 00:37:25,849
[Marko] Then cancel it,
you idiot.

585
00:37:25,949 --> 00:37:27,851
- [buttons click]
- Signal canceled, sir.

586
00:37:27,951 --> 00:37:29,185
We're okay.

587
00:37:29,285 --> 00:37:31,121
We're pretty fucking far
from okay.

588
00:37:31,221 --> 00:37:33,123
Now, get your sorry ass down
and disable the lifeboats

589
00:37:33,223 --> 00:37:34,224
so she can't get away.

590
00:37:34,324 --> 00:37:35,392
Yes, sir.

591
00:37:36,893 --> 00:37:38,061
And where the fuck is Jonathan?

592
00:37:38,161 --> 00:37:40,196
I'm on it, sir. Jorge, come in.

593
00:37:40,296 --> 00:37:42,733
[tense music continues]

594
00:37:53,877 --> 00:37:55,211
Ah! Fuck.

595
00:38:01,017 --> 00:38:02,318
Come on.

596
00:38:02,419 --> 00:38:03,520
Hey, you.

597
00:38:05,756 --> 00:38:07,223
You know how to use
one of these things?

598
00:38:07,323 --> 00:38:08,258
Yes.

599
00:38:09,259 --> 00:38:10,761
- Okay, listen.
- [Seng mumbles in Thai]

600
00:38:10,861 --> 00:38:12,496
I'm gonna look
for the woman who found you.

601
00:38:12,596 --> 00:38:14,264
I think she might be in trouble.

602
00:38:14,364 --> 00:38:16,567
- Don't wait for me.
- Okay.

603
00:38:28,712 --> 00:38:30,346
Captain on the bridge.

604
00:38:30,447 --> 00:38:31,682
[Spencer] As you were.

605
00:38:32,282 --> 00:38:34,317
- Good morning.
- Morning, sir.

606
00:38:34,417 --> 00:38:36,520
Distress call came in
from a cargo ship.

607
00:38:36,620 --> 00:38:38,455
KMG Artemis.

608
00:38:38,555 --> 00:38:40,156
Nine degrees, 49 minutes north,

609
00:38:40,256 --> 00:38:42,593
92 degrees, 56 minutes east.

610
00:38:42,693 --> 00:38:44,595
05:33 hours local time.

611
00:38:44,695 --> 00:38:47,297
That's the edge
of the Andaman Sea.

612
00:38:47,397 --> 00:38:49,600
- What was the code?
- Attack, sir.

613
00:38:50,366 --> 00:38:52,703
An attack? By who?

614
00:38:52,803 --> 00:38:54,538
Last I checked,
we were 600 miles east

615
00:38:54,638 --> 00:38:55,639
of any pirate activity.

616
00:38:55,739 --> 00:38:56,873
They canceled the call

617
00:38:56,973 --> 00:38:58,675
before we could respond.

618
00:38:58,775 --> 00:39:00,443
Must have been
some kind of mistake.

619
00:39:01,244 --> 00:39:02,946
[clicks tongue, inhales sharply]

620
00:39:03,046 --> 00:39:04,715
Let's give 'em a call back,
Yates.

621
00:39:04,815 --> 00:39:07,050
- Make sure everything's kosher.
- Yes, sir.

622
00:39:09,586 --> 00:39:11,021
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.

623
00:39:11,121 --> 00:39:14,525
This is the USS Hazard Perry
on Channel 16.

624
00:39:14,625 --> 00:39:16,359
[over radio]
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.

625
00:39:16,459 --> 00:39:19,730
This is the USS Hazard Perry
on Channel 16.

626
00:39:19,830 --> 00:39:21,565
-
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.
- Tsk.

627
00:39:22,298 --> 00:39:23,333
[radio beeps]

628
00:39:23,433 --> 00:39:25,301
Hazard Perry, this is Artemis.

629
00:39:26,903 --> 00:39:28,672
Good morning.
This is Captain Spencer

630
00:39:28,772 --> 00:39:31,174
of the USS Hazard Perry.
Who am I talking to?

631
00:39:31,742 --> 00:39:34,477
This is Marko Madsen,
captain of the Artemis.

632
00:39:34,578 --> 00:39:36,547
You must have gotten
our DSC call.

633
00:39:36,647 --> 00:39:37,681
[Spencer over radio]
Yeah, we sure did.

634
00:39:37,781 --> 00:39:38,915
So, what happened there?

635
00:39:39,449 --> 00:39:40,517
I'm sorry, one of my guys

636
00:39:40,617 --> 00:39:42,318
spotted light in our wake.

637
00:39:42,418 --> 00:39:43,820
He had a run-in
with some Somalis

638
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,221
a few years ago.

639
00:39:45,321 --> 00:39:46,289
You know how that goes.

640
00:39:46,389 --> 00:39:47,390
Got a little trigger-happy

641
00:39:47,490 --> 00:39:49,092
with the DSC.

642
00:39:49,192 --> 00:39:50,961
But it turns out,
it was just a fishing vessel.

643
00:39:53,764 --> 00:39:55,932
You're pretty far out for
a fishing vessel, aren't you?

644
00:39:57,467 --> 00:39:59,369
Must-- must have been
a deep-sea trawler.

645
00:39:59,469 --> 00:40:00,871
Not the first one we see.

646
00:40:02,839 --> 00:40:04,708
Sorry to waste the navy's time.

647
00:40:07,711 --> 00:40:10,146
Not at all.
Glad everyone's okay.

648
00:40:12,883 --> 00:40:13,850
[radio thuds]

649
00:40:16,152 --> 00:40:18,354
[Jamai] You have no idea
where he could be?

650
00:40:18,454 --> 00:40:19,590
No clue, I'm afraid.

651
00:40:19,690 --> 00:40:20,757
We have a call to you

652
00:40:20,857 --> 00:40:22,125
from a burner phone,

653
00:40:22,225 --> 00:40:24,094
shortly after the accident,

654
00:40:24,194 --> 00:40:25,295
near the port.

655
00:40:27,063 --> 00:40:28,131
Who called you?

656
00:40:29,532 --> 00:40:31,434
I... don't recall.

657
00:40:32,235 --> 00:40:33,970
To be honest, I--
I don't even remember

658
00:40:34,070 --> 00:40:35,205
receiving the phone call.

659
00:40:35,305 --> 00:40:37,307
There was a lot going on.

660
00:40:40,243 --> 00:40:41,578
Okay, well,

661
00:40:42,345 --> 00:40:45,015
please let us know
if you remember anything, or...

662
00:40:45,649 --> 00:40:47,751
if any further information
comes to light.

663
00:40:48,652 --> 00:40:50,053
As you can imagine,

664
00:40:50,854 --> 00:40:54,057
your father's murder
is our highest priority.

665
00:40:55,659 --> 00:40:57,027
Of course.

666
00:40:58,729 --> 00:41:00,997
[tense music]

667
00:41:15,712 --> 00:41:17,614
[indistinct murmuring]

668
00:41:17,714 --> 00:41:20,183
[running footsteps]

669
00:41:25,221 --> 00:41:26,790
[Angie grunts]

670
00:41:26,890 --> 00:41:28,859
[Cole shushing]

671
00:41:28,959 --> 00:41:30,727
[Cole] You're okay. Trust me.

672
00:41:31,561 --> 00:41:34,798
[Angie gasps, breathing heavily]

673
00:41:35,431 --> 00:41:36,466
[Cole] Open it.

674
00:41:37,067 --> 00:41:38,034
[Angie grunts]

675
00:41:40,303 --> 00:41:42,305
- [door closes]
- [lever handle clunks]

676
00:41:42,405 --> 00:41:43,674
[Angie] Who the fuck are you?

677
00:41:43,774 --> 00:41:45,175
I'm not one of them.

678
00:41:45,275 --> 00:41:46,442
Right now,
that's all that matters.

679
00:41:46,542 --> 00:41:47,610
[panting]

680
00:41:47,711 --> 00:41:49,112
There are people in the hold,

681
00:41:49,212 --> 00:41:50,280
and they're in danger.

682
00:41:50,380 --> 00:41:52,148
They're not gonna kill them,

683
00:41:52,248 --> 00:41:53,616
not when they're making money
off of them.

684
00:41:53,717 --> 00:41:54,718
You don't know
what they're gonna do.

685
00:41:54,818 --> 00:41:56,286
They shot me.

686
00:42:01,892 --> 00:42:02,959
[indistinct radio chatter]

687
00:42:05,662 --> 00:42:09,499
[woman speaks Thai]

688
00:42:09,599 --> 00:42:11,835
[migrants conversing in Thai]

689
00:42:15,672 --> 00:42:16,907
- [gunshot]
- [Dara] Aah!

690
00:42:17,007 --> 00:42:18,308
[migrants screaming]

691
00:42:18,408 --> 00:42:19,642
Check for more.

692
00:42:19,743 --> 00:42:21,511
Everybody, let's go!
Out of the lifeboat!

693
00:42:21,611 --> 00:42:23,379
[screaming continues]

694
00:42:23,947 --> 00:42:25,481
[Angie] We need to help them.

695
00:42:26,449 --> 00:42:27,884
[Cole] We will.

696
00:42:27,984 --> 00:42:30,186
But first, we need to take care
of that wound.

697
00:42:30,286 --> 00:42:32,488
Come. This way.

698
00:42:37,761 --> 00:42:39,295
Down there.

699
00:42:41,364 --> 00:42:44,434
[action music]

700
00:42:54,344 --> 00:42:55,712
[exhales sharply]

701
00:43:00,516 --> 00:43:01,952
[Diego hisses] Shit.

702
00:43:40,824 --> 00:43:43,359
[tense music]

703
00:43:52,502 --> 00:43:54,037
[groans]

704
00:43:56,106 --> 00:43:57,207
Come on.

705
00:44:00,676 --> 00:44:02,545
I found Jonathan's stuff
in a lifeboat.

706
00:44:05,916 --> 00:44:07,583
Josef and Simon are dead.

707
00:44:07,683 --> 00:44:09,352
- What?
- Yeah.

708
00:44:11,788 --> 00:44:13,156
They were serious players,
Captain.

709
00:44:13,256 --> 00:44:15,091
Whoever did this
had to be a professional.

710
00:44:15,191 --> 00:44:17,327
It can't be Ellis.
She's fleet navy.

711
00:44:17,427 --> 00:44:18,962
No combat experience.
And even if she did--

712
00:44:19,062 --> 00:44:21,297
[Marko] Still,
she took you out, right?

713
00:44:23,699 --> 00:44:24,935
Sweep the ship.

714
00:44:25,035 --> 00:44:27,037
Find out who the fuck's came on.

715
00:44:27,137 --> 00:44:28,238
Yes, Captain.

716
00:44:31,875 --> 00:44:33,810
[keypad beeping]

717
00:44:36,813 --> 00:44:38,481
We got a problem on the ship.

718
00:44:39,615 --> 00:44:42,218
[loud whirring]

719
00:44:51,461 --> 00:44:52,595
[grunts]

720
00:44:59,635 --> 00:45:00,770
[Angie] Here.

721
00:45:04,607 --> 00:45:06,576
[headsets beep]

722
00:45:06,676 --> 00:45:10,080
[Angie breathing heavily]

723
00:45:14,317 --> 00:45:15,986
[over headset] I've seen worse.

724
00:45:16,086 --> 00:45:17,687
[Angie] I saw you on the news.

725
00:45:18,654 --> 00:45:20,023
I know you're on the run.

726
00:45:20,456 --> 00:45:22,893
Are you at least gonna tell me
your name?

727
00:45:22,993 --> 00:45:24,327
Cole Reed.

728
00:45:24,427 --> 00:45:26,496
[sighs] Okay, Cole Reed.

729
00:45:26,596 --> 00:45:27,830
I'm Angie Ellis.

730
00:45:29,299 --> 00:45:30,967
Okay, Angie Ellis.

731
00:45:31,767 --> 00:45:33,870
This is gonna hurt.

732
00:45:33,970 --> 00:45:35,438
Maybe you wanna talk,
take your mind off of it.

733
00:45:35,538 --> 00:45:36,672
No. [exhales sharply]

734
00:45:36,772 --> 00:45:37,673
Tell me something
about yourself.

735
00:45:37,773 --> 00:45:39,242
[Angie breathes sharply]

736
00:45:39,342 --> 00:45:41,377
Aah! Fuck me!

737
00:45:41,477 --> 00:45:43,713
- You have a family?
- [breathes sharply]

738
00:45:43,813 --> 00:45:45,581
I have a deadbeat ex,

739
00:45:45,681 --> 00:45:47,617
and the most wonderful
little girl in the world.

740
00:45:49,119 --> 00:45:50,520
What's her name?

741
00:45:50,620 --> 00:45:51,687
[Angie] Violet.

742
00:45:53,056 --> 00:45:54,390
Great name.

743
00:45:54,490 --> 00:45:55,959
How old is she?

744
00:45:56,059 --> 00:45:58,294
[Angie breathes sharply]
She just turned six.

745
00:45:58,394 --> 00:46:00,463
[yells in pain]

746
00:46:00,563 --> 00:46:01,597
- Fuck!
- Try to hold still.

747
00:46:01,697 --> 00:46:02,999
[Angie] Oh!

748
00:46:03,633 --> 00:46:06,469
[Angie grunting]

749
00:46:06,569 --> 00:46:07,971
[relieved exhale]

750
00:46:08,071 --> 00:46:09,339
Fuck, that hurts!

751
00:46:10,240 --> 00:46:11,874
- Oh, fuck.
- [bullet clatters]

752
00:46:11,975 --> 00:46:13,109
[relieved sigh]

753
00:46:13,209 --> 00:46:15,378
Oh, my God. [exhales]

754
00:46:15,478 --> 00:46:17,547
[Cole] Share custody
with Mr. Deadbeat Ex?

755
00:46:19,082 --> 00:46:20,516
[Angie] No.

756
00:46:20,616 --> 00:46:21,985
[inhales sharply]

757
00:46:22,085 --> 00:46:23,319
Oh!

758
00:46:23,419 --> 00:46:25,288
I used to share partial custody,

759
00:46:25,388 --> 00:46:27,590
but then I lost it
when I got fired from the navy.

760
00:46:28,691 --> 00:46:30,760
[breathes deeply]

761
00:46:30,860 --> 00:46:32,795
I promised her I'd be back
more than two days a month,

762
00:46:32,895 --> 00:46:34,965
and I--
I can't even fucking do that.

763
00:46:35,531 --> 00:46:37,533
[sighs] There's still time.

764
00:46:40,370 --> 00:46:42,905
- Okay.
- [grunts]

765
00:46:43,006 --> 00:46:44,507
[breathes deeply]

766
00:46:52,682 --> 00:46:54,284
I need backup
at the engine room.

767
00:46:56,286 --> 00:46:58,354
- Oh. Yeah.
- [Cole] Okay?

768
00:46:58,454 --> 00:46:59,655
- We need to keep moving.
- Okay, I got it.

769
00:46:59,755 --> 00:47:02,658
Yeah. I got it. I'm good.

770
00:47:02,758 --> 00:47:05,428
[loud whirring]

771
00:47:19,042 --> 00:47:20,977
[over headset] She was here.
She couldn't have got far.

772
00:47:21,077 --> 00:47:22,312
Move.

773
00:47:32,888 --> 00:47:34,857
Any fishing boat this far out

774
00:47:34,957 --> 00:47:36,626
would be registered
on AIS, right?

775
00:47:37,160 --> 00:47:38,194
Yes, sir.

776
00:47:38,294 --> 00:47:39,495
Let's check and see what traffic

777
00:47:39,595 --> 00:47:40,963
was near the Artemis's position

778
00:47:41,064 --> 00:47:42,965
- around the time of the call.
- Sir.

779
00:47:43,066 --> 00:47:44,567
And, uh, see
what you can drum up

780
00:47:44,667 --> 00:47:47,437
on this Captain Marko Madsen.

781
00:47:58,114 --> 00:47:59,382
Hey, hey.

782
00:47:59,482 --> 00:48:01,084
What happened in Bangkok?

783
00:48:01,184 --> 00:48:02,752
On the news, they said
you're Campallo's bodyguard.

784
00:48:02,852 --> 00:48:05,388
Did you kill him?
Did you kill those cops?

785
00:48:05,488 --> 00:48:07,023
Why are you on the ship?

786
00:48:07,123 --> 00:48:08,458
That is not what happened.

787
00:48:10,260 --> 00:48:11,594
Right now, all that matters
is we get you

788
00:48:11,694 --> 00:48:13,029
and those people to safety.

789
00:48:14,830 --> 00:48:16,399
I sent out a distress signal.

790
00:48:16,499 --> 00:48:17,700
I don't know if anyone got it.

791
00:48:18,434 --> 00:48:20,270
There's no cell service
on the ship, but I know

792
00:48:20,370 --> 00:48:22,538
that there are sat phones
and radios on the bridge.

793
00:48:22,638 --> 00:48:23,906
Then that's where we need to go.

794
00:48:24,006 --> 00:48:25,075
If we go to the bridge,
every man on the ship

795
00:48:25,175 --> 00:48:26,276
will come running.

796
00:48:26,776 --> 00:48:28,010
[sighs]

797
00:48:28,111 --> 00:48:29,779
We need a diversion.

798
00:48:32,182 --> 00:48:34,050
[tense music]

799
00:48:34,150 --> 00:48:35,485
[Angie] In the last cargo hold.

800
00:48:36,586 --> 00:48:37,653
This way.

801
00:48:42,825 --> 00:48:43,893
It's here.

802
00:48:46,862 --> 00:48:48,931
- [handle clanks, squeaks]
- [Angie grunts]

803
00:48:49,031 --> 00:48:50,400
- [Angie] Ah.
- Here, let me help.

804
00:48:51,067 --> 00:48:53,303
[handle clunks]

805
00:48:54,237 --> 00:48:57,973
[doors squeaking]

806
00:48:59,909 --> 00:49:01,577
[Cole] What about the refugees?

807
00:49:01,677 --> 00:49:03,313
In an emergency,
every section of this boat

808
00:49:03,413 --> 00:49:04,447
can be sealed off.

809
00:49:04,547 --> 00:49:05,715
They'll be safe.

810
00:49:13,589 --> 00:49:15,558
[ripping]

811
00:49:21,664 --> 00:49:23,666
- [lighter closes]
- Let's go.

812
00:49:23,766 --> 00:49:26,336
[tense music]

813
00:49:37,447 --> 00:49:38,881
[indistinct radio chatter]

814
00:49:42,252 --> 00:49:44,787
[fire crackling]

815
00:49:46,389 --> 00:49:51,694
[alarm blaring]

816
00:49:51,794 --> 00:49:53,629
Fire on five. Seal it off.

817
00:49:54,096 --> 00:49:55,865
- Initiate fire protocol.
- [buttons click]

818
00:49:56,766 --> 00:49:57,967
Listen up, everybody.

819
00:49:58,067 --> 00:50:00,270
This is a diversion.

820
00:50:00,370 --> 00:50:01,704
We have a stowaway.

821
00:50:01,804 --> 00:50:04,607
I want two guards
at each tower door.

822
00:50:05,541 --> 00:50:08,878
Diego, I want you to oversee
and patrol the towers.

823
00:50:08,978 --> 00:50:10,880
- Yes, sir.
- [Marko] Mateo,

824
00:50:10,980 --> 00:50:12,282
you go down with the fire team.

825
00:50:12,382 --> 00:50:13,783
I'll surveil the deck.

826
00:50:13,883 --> 00:50:14,950
Yes, sir.

827
00:50:15,050 --> 00:50:17,287
[tense music continues]

828
00:50:19,422 --> 00:50:20,456
[gun cocks]

829
00:50:38,908 --> 00:50:40,075
[crewman]
A fire on the high seas.

830
00:50:40,176 --> 00:50:41,411
That's definitely
the worst thing

831
00:50:41,511 --> 00:50:42,745
you can have out here.

832
00:50:44,947 --> 00:50:46,649
[fire roaring]

833
00:50:46,749 --> 00:50:48,083
Increase pressure!

834
00:50:56,426 --> 00:50:57,693
- [loud clang]
- [exhales]

835
00:50:59,795 --> 00:51:01,997
[fire continues roaring]

836
00:51:02,097 --> 00:51:03,866
- It's the batteries, sir.
- [Marko over radio]
Contain it.

837
00:51:03,966 --> 00:51:05,100
I'm going up top.

838
00:51:06,702 --> 00:51:09,505
[tense music continues]

839
00:51:14,277 --> 00:51:16,712
[breathing heavily]

840
00:51:47,377 --> 00:51:48,678
[loud clang]

841
00:52:12,935 --> 00:52:14,470
[crewman 1 gasps, grunts]

842
00:52:14,570 --> 00:52:16,639
[crewman 1] Aah!
[grunts in pain]

843
00:52:16,739 --> 00:52:18,441
- [grunts]
- [bones snap]

844
00:52:18,541 --> 00:52:20,276
- [body thuds]
- [radio static crackles]

845
00:52:23,446 --> 00:52:24,814
[beeping]

846
00:52:24,914 --> 00:52:26,181
Mayday, Mayday, Mayday.

847
00:52:26,282 --> 00:52:28,551
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

848
00:52:29,785 --> 00:52:31,587
All posts report.

849
00:52:31,687 --> 00:52:33,122
All posts report.

850
00:52:33,589 --> 00:52:35,124
Portside secure, sir.

851
00:52:35,224 --> 00:52:36,526
[crewman 2 over radio]
Starboard
entrance is secure, sir.

852
00:52:36,626 --> 00:52:39,094
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

853
00:52:39,194 --> 00:52:40,363
[Mateo]
Fire contained, Captain.

854
00:52:40,463 --> 00:52:42,432
Seal the hold. Return to deck.

855
00:52:45,701 --> 00:52:48,538
[Angie] This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 9.

856
00:52:48,638 --> 00:52:50,239
Please respond.

857
00:52:53,042 --> 00:52:55,110
This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 16.

858
00:52:55,210 --> 00:52:56,746
Please respond.

859
00:52:57,279 --> 00:52:59,649
Captain to bridge. Report.

860
00:53:01,817 --> 00:53:03,819
We're about to be short on time.

861
00:53:07,256 --> 00:53:08,524
Captain to bridge.

862
00:53:08,624 --> 00:53:09,692
Report.

863
00:53:09,792 --> 00:53:11,561
- Shit.
- [beeps]

864
00:53:15,097 --> 00:53:17,066
[tense music intensifies]

865
00:53:17,166 --> 00:53:18,401
[exhales sharply]

866
00:53:21,136 --> 00:53:23,406
They're on the bridge.
Diego, get up there.

867
00:53:26,141 --> 00:53:27,443
[footsteps]

868
00:53:29,345 --> 00:53:30,580
[Cole] Keep quiet.

869
00:53:31,914 --> 00:53:34,984
[suspenseful music]

870
00:53:46,195 --> 00:53:49,331
This is Captain Spencer
of the USS Hazard Perry.

871
00:53:49,432 --> 00:53:51,100
[Diego exclaims, yells]

872
00:53:52,835 --> 00:53:55,304
[Diego grunting]

873
00:53:57,172 --> 00:53:59,341
[radio feedback squeals,
static crackles]

874
00:53:59,442 --> 00:54:01,076
[Angie] Commander Spencer,
this is the KMG Artemis.

875
00:54:01,176 --> 00:54:02,712
We need immediate
emergency assistance.

876
00:54:02,812 --> 00:54:03,946
[Marko shouting indistinctly]

877
00:54:04,046 --> 00:54:05,548
Who am I talking to
and who is "we"?

878
00:54:05,648 --> 00:54:07,016
[over radio]
My name is Angie Ellis.

879
00:54:07,116 --> 00:54:08,784
I'm the third mate
on the Artemis.

880
00:54:08,884 --> 00:54:11,286
I'm with a man named Cole Reed.
We need help.

881
00:54:12,221 --> 00:54:14,223
The captain is running
a human trafficking operation.

882
00:54:14,323 --> 00:54:16,959
Our position
is latitude 45 degrees north,

883
00:54:17,059 --> 00:54:18,861
- longitude 155 east.
- We need to move.

884
00:54:18,961 --> 00:54:21,363
- Now.
- Send help! Fast!

885
00:54:25,367 --> 00:54:26,936
[Yates] Was that gunfire, sir?

886
00:54:27,036 --> 00:54:28,571
Get me that dossier. Now.

887
00:54:28,671 --> 00:54:30,606
- Set course for the Artemis.
- Yes, sir.

888
00:54:30,706 --> 00:54:33,409
[tense music]

889
00:54:36,211 --> 00:54:37,880
[Angie] Come on.
We're going to my cabin.

890
00:54:42,084 --> 00:54:43,586
We should be able
to get down from here.

891
00:54:43,686 --> 00:54:45,755
[indistinct radio chatter]

892
00:54:49,191 --> 00:54:50,526
[Cole] They're right outside.

893
00:54:55,030 --> 00:54:58,634
[breathing shakily]

894
00:54:58,734 --> 00:55:00,402
[Angie] If I-- If I don't...

895
00:55:01,170 --> 00:55:02,404
Oh, God.

896
00:55:02,505 --> 00:55:03,706
[Cole] Here, sit.

897
00:55:05,908 --> 00:55:07,743
- Look at me.
- [continues breathing shakily]

898
00:55:07,843 --> 00:55:09,244
I'm gonna get you back to her.

899
00:55:10,245 --> 00:55:11,380
I promise.

900
00:55:12,247 --> 00:55:14,584
Mm. Okay.

901
00:55:14,684 --> 00:55:16,919
[tense music continues]

902
00:55:26,729 --> 00:55:28,097
Bigger cut for each of us.

903
00:55:30,032 --> 00:55:31,701
All right, listen up.

904
00:55:31,801 --> 00:55:33,168
There is no stowaway.

905
00:55:33,268 --> 00:55:34,637
That's Campallo's bodyguard.

906
00:55:35,204 --> 00:55:37,139
[over radio]
So, there's a change of plans.

907
00:55:37,239 --> 00:55:40,175
Going in two hours,
ship to ship.

908
00:55:40,275 --> 00:55:41,844
- What's in two hours?
- I don't know.

909
00:55:41,944 --> 00:55:43,445
- [Marko] Understood?
- [all] Yes, sir.

910
00:55:43,546 --> 00:55:44,480
Move.

911
00:55:55,958 --> 00:55:58,728
[phone buzzing]

912
00:56:01,430 --> 00:56:03,032
Go ahead.

913
00:56:03,132 --> 00:56:04,333
[Marko over phone]
What the fuck is Cole Reed

914
00:56:04,433 --> 00:56:06,401
doing on my ship, huh?

915
00:56:06,502 --> 00:56:08,270
How is he even alive?

916
00:56:09,004 --> 00:56:11,106
I thought we took care of him
when we killed Tibu.

917
00:56:12,074 --> 00:56:13,242
What the fuck's going on?

918
00:56:14,977 --> 00:56:17,312
Look, the kill team fucked up.

919
00:56:18,347 --> 00:56:20,883
Don't let him fuck up
the transaction.

920
00:56:20,983 --> 00:56:23,485
He won't.
We moved up the delivery.

921
00:56:23,586 --> 00:56:25,187
I've contacted Bertus.

922
00:56:25,287 --> 00:56:27,089
He's two hours away.

923
00:56:27,189 --> 00:56:28,157
Fine.

924
00:56:28,691 --> 00:56:30,192
Just make sure that Cole Reed

925
00:56:30,292 --> 00:56:32,061
doesn't get off that ship alive.

926
00:56:32,161 --> 00:56:33,395
I will.

927
00:56:33,495 --> 00:56:34,564
You're gonna owe me extra

928
00:56:34,664 --> 00:56:36,165
for dealing with this thug.

929
00:56:36,265 --> 00:56:38,100
Any updates on Kameron?

930
00:56:38,701 --> 00:56:40,435
Are we still in business?

931
00:56:41,170 --> 00:56:42,471
The sale has been halted.

932
00:56:43,606 --> 00:56:44,840
It's business as usual.

933
00:56:46,609 --> 00:56:47,677
What is it?

934
00:56:47,777 --> 00:56:48,878
Who's Kameron?

935
00:56:50,045 --> 00:56:51,346
Kameron's Tibu's son.

936
00:56:51,446 --> 00:56:52,882
And you think he's involved?

937
00:56:52,982 --> 00:56:54,049
I don't know.

938
00:56:54,984 --> 00:56:56,385
But Marko's involved.

939
00:56:57,186 --> 00:56:58,554
- And he's gonna pay.
- [crewman] Move.

940
00:56:59,722 --> 00:57:01,056
Couldn't have got far.

941
00:57:01,857 --> 00:57:03,292
It's time to go.

942
00:57:08,130 --> 00:57:11,166
[tense music]

943
00:57:12,868 --> 00:57:14,236
[Angie grunts]

944
00:57:14,336 --> 00:57:15,905
[gunshots]

945
00:57:19,141 --> 00:57:21,577
[wind whooshing]

946
00:57:27,149 --> 00:57:29,919
[Cole]
Until the navy gets here,
those migrants aren't safe.

947
00:57:30,352 --> 00:57:31,787
We need to get below deck.

948
00:57:31,887 --> 00:57:33,288
There are lots of places
to hide 'em down there,

949
00:57:33,388 --> 00:57:34,489
but you heard him,

950
00:57:34,590 --> 00:57:35,725
they're all being guarded.

951
00:57:36,592 --> 00:57:37,893
There's gotta be another way.

952
00:57:39,328 --> 00:57:41,597
We could try
the ventilation shaft.

953
00:57:42,898 --> 00:57:45,000
Sir, the dossier you requested.

954
00:57:45,601 --> 00:57:48,570
Marko's been with KMG
for 13 years, captain for ten.

955
00:57:49,104 --> 00:57:50,740
Danish national, Jaeger Corps.

956
00:57:50,840 --> 00:57:52,141
Tours in Afghanistan, Iraq.

957
00:57:52,241 --> 00:57:53,609
Investigated twice.

958
00:57:53,709 --> 00:57:55,510
Allegations of looting
and smuggling.

959
00:57:56,078 --> 00:57:58,147
They thought he killed one
of his teammates on a mission,

960
00:57:58,247 --> 00:57:59,615
but the rest of the unit
wasn't talking.

961
00:57:59,715 --> 00:58:01,784
- Nothing stuck.
- And his crew?

962
00:58:01,884 --> 00:58:05,154
Half of them are either
ex-military or ex-mercenary.

963
00:58:05,254 --> 00:58:06,689
Spanish MEO,

964
00:58:06,789 --> 00:58:09,324
Irish AOW, GRU.

965
00:58:09,424 --> 00:58:11,260
What about the man
that Angie said she was with,

966
00:58:11,360 --> 00:58:12,895
uh, Cole Reed?

967
00:58:12,995 --> 00:58:15,030
- Anything on him?
- Not on the company roster.

968
00:58:15,130 --> 00:58:16,932
But wait till you see this.

969
00:58:17,032 --> 00:58:18,500
[reporter on monitor]
The suspect is very dangerous

970
00:58:18,600 --> 00:58:20,202
and still on the loose.

971
00:58:20,302 --> 00:58:22,537
A citywide order to shelter
is in place

972
00:58:22,638 --> 00:58:24,974
until he is apprehended.

973
00:58:25,074 --> 00:58:27,076
A cop-killing fugitive.

974
00:58:27,877 --> 00:58:29,544
You have gotta be kidding me.

975
00:58:30,612 --> 00:58:32,815
Just what this shitshow
was missing.

976
00:58:34,416 --> 00:58:36,218
Get me satellite footage
of that ship.

977
00:58:36,318 --> 00:58:37,552
[Yates] Yes, sir.

978
00:58:38,387 --> 00:58:40,890
[metal creaking]

979
00:58:44,126 --> 00:58:45,327
[Angie grunts, strains]

980
00:58:45,427 --> 00:58:47,629
[wind whooshing]

981
00:58:47,730 --> 00:58:48,764
[Angie grunts]

982
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,940
[action music]

983
00:59:02,444 --> 00:59:03,512
[Cole grunts]

984
00:59:07,983 --> 00:59:09,785
[Spencer] Well, shit.

985
00:59:11,253 --> 00:59:13,022
Tell me that's not an MP5.

986
00:59:14,423 --> 00:59:15,524
Sir.

987
00:59:16,125 --> 00:59:18,127
I hear there's a fugitive
on board.

988
00:59:18,861 --> 00:59:19,962
We know if he's a friendly?

989
00:59:21,163 --> 00:59:22,597
Friendly or not,

990
00:59:22,698 --> 00:59:24,399
make sure your men
are good to go.

991
00:59:24,499 --> 00:59:26,101
We launch
as soon as they're ready.

992
00:59:27,336 --> 00:59:28,303
Sir.

993
00:59:32,674 --> 00:59:34,043
[action music continues]

994
00:59:34,143 --> 00:59:35,110
[strains]

995
00:59:43,052 --> 00:59:45,054
[crewman] I think
I heard something over here.

996
00:59:46,956 --> 00:59:49,558
- Over there!
- Cole, someone's coming.

997
00:59:49,658 --> 00:59:51,861
- [metal creaking]
- [flashlight button clicks]

998
00:59:51,961 --> 00:59:54,196
[tense music]

999
00:59:58,968 --> 01:00:01,804
- [gunshots]
- [bullets ricocheting]

1000
01:00:02,872 --> 01:00:05,340
- [scraping]
- Shit! [grunting]

1001
01:00:10,679 --> 01:00:13,148
[panting]

1002
01:00:16,685 --> 01:00:19,554
[wind whooshing]

1003
01:00:25,995 --> 01:00:28,097
[metal creaking]

1004
01:00:29,999 --> 01:00:31,533
[Cole breathing heavily]

1005
01:00:52,888 --> 01:00:53,889
[metal creaks]

1006
01:00:55,257 --> 01:00:57,526
[breathing heavily]

1007
01:00:57,626 --> 01:00:58,861
[thuds lightly]

1008
01:00:58,961 --> 01:01:00,595
[clanging echoes]

1009
01:01:02,297 --> 01:01:05,767
[gunshots]

1010
01:01:05,868 --> 01:01:08,537
[scraping, creaking]

1011
01:01:08,637 --> 01:01:09,638
[muffled thud]

1012
01:01:11,573 --> 01:01:13,475
[metal groaning]

1013
01:01:13,575 --> 01:01:14,810
[cover clatters]

1014
01:01:28,723 --> 01:01:29,925
[Angie grunts]

1015
01:01:31,593 --> 01:01:32,661
Now, we're even.

1016
01:01:36,765 --> 01:01:38,333
[crewman over radio]
Captain, we shot the stowaway

1017
01:01:38,433 --> 01:01:40,202
through the vent shaft,
heard him drop.

1018
01:01:40,302 --> 01:01:41,503
Don't know if we hit him.

1019
01:01:41,603 --> 01:01:42,637
[Marko]
Block the hole.

1020
01:01:42,737 --> 01:01:44,206
Return to deck.

1021
01:01:44,306 --> 01:01:46,541
I'll take care
of this guy myself.

1022
01:01:46,641 --> 01:01:47,609
Copy.

1023
01:01:49,478 --> 01:01:51,513
[Angie exhales sharply] Fuck.

1024
01:01:51,613 --> 01:01:52,848
[glass crunches]

1025
01:01:54,349 --> 01:01:55,450
Oh.

1026
01:01:58,820 --> 01:02:00,489
I'd like to see you twirl now.

1027
01:02:01,323 --> 01:02:02,457
Sit down.

1028
01:02:04,459 --> 01:02:05,928
The four of you, with me.

1029
01:02:06,028 --> 01:02:08,898
- Everybody else, fan out.
- [crunches]

1030
01:02:09,431 --> 01:02:11,066
- You keep an eye on her.
- Yes, sir.

1031
01:02:11,166 --> 01:02:12,834
[Marko] Let's go.

1032
01:02:12,935 --> 01:02:14,203
[Spencer] How far are we?

1033
01:02:14,303 --> 01:02:15,337
[Turner] Forty-two miles, sir.

1034
01:02:15,437 --> 01:02:16,371
Time?

1035
01:02:16,471 --> 01:02:18,040
Seventy-five minutes, sir.

1036
01:02:18,840 --> 01:02:19,942
Launch the VBSS crew.

1037
01:02:20,042 --> 01:02:21,210
Yes, sir.

1038
01:02:21,310 --> 01:02:24,146
[action music]

1039
01:02:27,549 --> 01:02:28,550
[hatch opens]

1040
01:02:29,218 --> 01:02:31,820
[engine revving]

1041
01:02:51,173 --> 01:02:52,707
[action music continues]

1042
01:02:52,807 --> 01:02:55,077
[engine revving]

1043
01:03:17,166 --> 01:03:19,068
[exhales sharply]

1044
01:03:19,834 --> 01:03:22,938
- [gunshot]
- [electricity crackling]

1045
01:03:23,038 --> 01:03:27,509
[alarm blaring]

1046
01:03:29,911 --> 01:03:31,780
[alarm continues blaring]

1047
01:03:31,880 --> 01:03:34,349
[suspenseful music]

1048
01:03:35,050 --> 01:03:36,185
[inhales]

1049
01:03:57,439 --> 01:04:01,977
[alarm blaring faintly]

1050
01:04:02,077 --> 01:04:06,448
[blaring intensifies]

1051
01:04:09,451 --> 01:04:11,320
- [squeaks]
- [lock clicks]

1052
01:04:11,420 --> 01:04:12,621
[exhales loudly]

1053
01:04:12,721 --> 01:04:13,989
He's trapped.

1054
01:04:14,089 --> 01:04:15,390
We'll deal with him later.

1055
01:04:16,125 --> 01:04:17,326
Captain to bridge.

1056
01:04:18,060 --> 01:04:20,395
- Lock off cargo hold three.
- [crewman over radio]
Sir.

1057
01:04:26,001 --> 01:04:28,770
- [metal groaning]
- [straining]

1058
01:04:33,275 --> 01:04:35,610
- [groaning continues]
- [straining]

1059
01:04:36,478 --> 01:04:39,848
[groaning continues]

1060
01:04:44,186 --> 01:04:45,354
[thud]

1061
01:04:47,022 --> 01:04:50,692
[clattering]

1062
01:04:52,861 --> 01:04:55,764
[clanging]

1063
01:04:55,864 --> 01:04:56,998
[grunts]

1064
01:04:57,099 --> 01:05:00,702
[thudding, clanging]

1065
01:05:00,802 --> 01:05:02,671
Got the intel package
on Cole Reed.

1066
01:05:02,771 --> 01:05:03,838
That'll be all.

1067
01:05:06,108 --> 01:05:08,543
[Underwood] Cole Reed,
born and raised in London.

1068
01:05:08,643 --> 01:05:10,179
Mom passed when he was seven.

1069
01:05:10,279 --> 01:05:12,347
Father was a cop.
Grandfather was a cop.

1070
01:05:12,447 --> 01:05:14,683
Finishes school,
goes right into the navy.

1071
01:05:14,783 --> 01:05:16,017
Royal Marines Commando.

1072
01:05:16,118 --> 01:05:17,852
Two tours in Afghanistan.

1073
01:05:17,952 --> 01:05:20,422
Comes home,
joins the London police.

1074
01:05:20,522 --> 01:05:23,758
Police Combat Cross for acts
of extraordinary heroism

1075
01:05:23,858 --> 01:05:25,360
while engaged
in personal combat

1076
01:05:25,460 --> 01:05:26,928
with an armed adversary.

1077
01:05:27,028 --> 01:05:28,597
Meritorious Police Duty Award

1078
01:05:28,697 --> 01:05:30,432
for an act
of extraordinary bravery

1079
01:05:30,532 --> 01:05:32,867
intelligently performed
in the line of duty.

1080
01:05:35,470 --> 01:05:37,239
Ends up serving under his dad

1081
01:05:37,339 --> 01:05:40,809
in the high-speed SCO19
Specialist Firearms Command.

1082
01:05:41,376 --> 01:05:43,212
His unit was stalking
a mob operation.

1083
01:05:43,312 --> 01:05:45,480
On the takedown night,
Reed went too far,

1084
01:05:45,580 --> 01:05:48,049
disobeyed orders,
got himself stuck inside.

1085
01:05:48,517 --> 01:05:51,586
His father went in to save him
and was shot and killed.

1086
01:05:52,321 --> 01:05:53,322
Wait a second.

1087
01:05:53,422 --> 01:05:54,556
His father was killed

1088
01:05:54,656 --> 01:05:55,657
saving him?

1089
01:05:55,757 --> 01:05:56,925
[Underwood] Yes, sir.

1090
01:05:57,692 --> 01:05:58,827
[Spencer] Jesus.

1091
01:06:00,695 --> 01:06:02,764
So, why'd he leave the UK?

1092
01:06:02,864 --> 01:06:04,333
[Underwood]
File goes cold.

1093
01:06:04,433 --> 01:06:05,934
A lot of people looking
for payback,

1094
01:06:06,034 --> 01:06:08,937
and, well...
he has no family left.

1095
01:06:09,037 --> 01:06:11,340
[Spencer breathes deeply]

1096
01:06:12,507 --> 01:06:16,010
I'll bet my pension
and my '67 Shelby

1097
01:06:16,111 --> 01:06:18,547
that whoever killed Campallo
is on that boat...

1098
01:06:19,881 --> 01:06:22,117
and Cole Reed is there
to square things up.

1099
01:06:22,217 --> 01:06:24,453
[tense music]

1100
01:06:31,025 --> 01:06:35,564
[singing in Thai]

1101
01:06:40,969 --> 01:06:43,505
[breathes heavily]

1102
01:06:43,605 --> 01:06:46,375
[breathes sharply]

1103
01:06:57,386 --> 01:07:01,756
[metal squeaks, creaking]

1104
01:07:02,624 --> 01:07:03,792
[gasps softly]

1105
01:07:06,595 --> 01:07:10,299
[ship horn blaring]

1106
01:07:15,237 --> 01:07:18,607
[ship horn blaring]

1107
01:07:32,854 --> 01:07:35,424
- [thudding]
- [sniffles]

1108
01:07:47,269 --> 01:07:48,603
[Marko] Lower the gangway.

1109
01:07:49,371 --> 01:07:50,672
- Lowering gangway.
- [button clicks]

1110
01:07:51,273 --> 01:07:53,875
[whirring]

1111
01:08:00,649 --> 01:08:02,784
[metal groaning]

1112
01:08:07,689 --> 01:08:09,791
[squeaks]

1113
01:08:13,395 --> 01:08:15,964
[phone ringtone playing]

1114
01:08:19,200 --> 01:08:20,402
Did the funds hit?

1115
01:08:25,807 --> 01:08:27,609
Funds confirmed.

1116
01:08:27,709 --> 01:08:30,044
What about our problem?

1117
01:08:31,880 --> 01:08:33,382
It's been contained.

1118
01:08:39,321 --> 01:08:40,822
Let's go and meet our guests.

1119
01:08:42,824 --> 01:08:45,827
[intriguing music]

1120
01:08:58,507 --> 01:08:59,708
Take them to the cargo.

1121
01:09:02,511 --> 01:09:04,846
- Ah, Cap.
- [Marko] Bertus.

1122
01:09:04,946 --> 01:09:06,348
[Bertus] Let's do it.

1123
01:09:06,915 --> 01:09:09,284
I saw smoke coming
from your ship on the way in.

1124
01:09:10,619 --> 01:09:11,953
Oh, yeah?

1125
01:09:12,053 --> 01:09:13,021
Well, what happens on my ship

1126
01:09:13,121 --> 01:09:14,155
is none of your business.

1127
01:09:14,255 --> 01:09:15,290
[Bertus chuckles]

1128
01:09:17,959 --> 01:09:20,094
- You wanna do this or what?
- Yeah.

1129
01:09:20,194 --> 01:09:21,563
Let's go inspect the goods.

1130
01:09:23,097 --> 01:09:24,899
I need to find myself
a clean one.

1131
01:09:25,967 --> 01:09:28,036
Best part of this job
is the ride home.

1132
01:09:28,970 --> 01:09:31,306
- Get in.
- [woman yelps]

1133
01:09:31,406 --> 01:09:32,407
Move.

1134
01:09:35,944 --> 01:09:37,078
[crewman] Get in there.

1135
01:09:47,656 --> 01:09:50,559
[thudding, clattering]

1136
01:09:50,659 --> 01:09:51,760
Thank you, Tibu.

1137
01:09:54,396 --> 01:09:57,065
[straining]

1138
01:10:00,301 --> 01:10:01,736
[sighs]

1139
01:10:02,571 --> 01:10:04,506
[metal creaking]

1140
01:10:05,273 --> 01:10:08,443
[action music]

1141
01:10:21,155 --> 01:10:23,458
[engine rumbling]

1142
01:10:25,527 --> 01:10:27,829
[grunting]

1143
01:10:43,678 --> 01:10:46,214
[light bulb buzzing]

1144
01:10:56,791 --> 01:10:59,060
[suspenseful music]

1145
01:11:04,799 --> 01:11:07,235
[ominous music]

1146
01:11:09,370 --> 01:11:12,373
[breathing sharply]

1147
01:11:16,578 --> 01:11:18,780
[grunting]

1148
01:11:18,880 --> 01:11:21,716
- Aah! [grunting]
- [strap creaking]

1149
01:11:21,816 --> 01:11:23,051
- [Cole grunts]
- [body thuds]

1150
01:11:23,151 --> 01:11:26,020
[intense music]

1151
01:11:31,493 --> 01:11:32,427
[Angie grunts]

1152
01:11:37,699 --> 01:11:38,767
[woman whimpering]

1153
01:11:38,867 --> 01:11:39,901
Here they are.

1154
01:11:42,003 --> 01:11:43,605
Now, get 'em off my ship.

1155
01:11:45,607 --> 01:11:46,908
- [crewmen grunt]
- [body thuds]

1156
01:11:47,008 --> 01:11:48,109
[gun cocks]

1157
01:11:48,209 --> 01:11:49,410
[Bertus]
What the fuck is going on?

1158
01:11:49,511 --> 01:11:51,412
[migrants gasp, whimper]

1159
01:11:56,217 --> 01:11:57,552
We have a stowaway.

1160
01:11:58,386 --> 01:11:59,688
A stowaway?

1161
01:11:59,788 --> 01:12:00,789
Yeah.

1162
01:12:01,255 --> 01:12:02,524
Well, what happens on your ship

1163
01:12:02,624 --> 01:12:04,358
is my fucking business now.

1164
01:12:04,459 --> 01:12:05,527
Calm down.

1165
01:12:05,627 --> 01:12:08,362
Everybody, calm down. Okay?

1166
01:12:08,463 --> 01:12:10,431
I will fix it. Calm down.

1167
01:12:12,366 --> 01:12:16,104
Boys, go down
and take care of this guy. Now.

1168
01:12:16,204 --> 01:12:17,706
Go! Go, go, go!

1169
01:12:19,440 --> 01:12:21,142
Mateo, go to the bridge

1170
01:12:21,242 --> 01:12:23,177
and deal with that bitch
once and for all.

1171
01:12:23,277 --> 01:12:24,979
- You understand?
- Yes, sir.

1172
01:12:27,281 --> 01:12:28,650
[clunks]

1173
01:12:28,750 --> 01:12:30,284
[door groaning]

1174
01:12:31,720 --> 01:12:34,055
[breathing sharply]

1175
01:12:35,557 --> 01:12:36,891
[door groans]

1176
01:12:36,991 --> 01:12:37,959
[gasps]

1177
01:12:44,899 --> 01:12:47,068
- [crewman grunting]
- [gunshots]

1178
01:12:47,168 --> 01:12:48,469
- [blood spurts]
- [body thuds]

1179
01:12:49,337 --> 01:12:52,006
[tense music]

1180
01:13:05,019 --> 01:13:06,688
[Angie grunts]

1181
01:13:09,524 --> 01:13:11,025
[indistinct radio chatter]

1182
01:13:12,694 --> 01:13:14,228
[crunches]

1183
01:13:14,328 --> 01:13:17,431
[crewman yelling,
grunts in pain]

1184
01:13:17,532 --> 01:13:20,702
- [crewman groans, grunts]
- [glass crackles]

1185
01:13:23,437 --> 01:13:26,040
[panting]

1186
01:13:27,141 --> 01:13:29,844
[running footsteps]

1187
01:13:30,779 --> 01:13:32,046
- [Mateo] Aah!
- [body thuds]

1188
01:13:32,146 --> 01:13:33,114
Fucker.

1189
01:13:33,548 --> 01:13:35,850
[breathing heavily]

1190
01:13:38,887 --> 01:13:41,222
[tense music continues]

1191
01:13:53,835 --> 01:13:57,739
[grunting]

1192
01:13:57,839 --> 01:13:58,740
Aah!

1193
01:13:58,840 --> 01:14:01,409
[grunting]

1194
01:14:01,509 --> 01:14:04,746
- [Cole grunting]
- [crewman 1 groans]

1195
01:14:06,014 --> 01:14:06,915
[grunts]

1196
01:14:07,015 --> 01:14:08,516
[crewman 2 grunting]

1197
01:14:10,251 --> 01:14:11,319
[grunts]

1198
01:14:12,253 --> 01:14:13,221
[grunts]

1199
01:14:14,422 --> 01:14:15,389
[body thuds]

1200
01:14:17,558 --> 01:14:18,526
[whispering] Shh.

1201
01:14:19,527 --> 01:14:20,629
Go to the stairs.

1202
01:14:20,729 --> 01:14:22,096
I'll go. Yeah?

1203
01:14:36,377 --> 01:14:39,547
[suspenseful music]

1204
01:14:40,348 --> 01:14:42,350
- [exhales sharply]
- [door creaks]

1205
01:14:43,852 --> 01:14:46,120
[grunting]

1206
01:14:47,922 --> 01:14:49,791
[grunting]

1207
01:14:50,391 --> 01:14:51,459
- [bones snap]
- [grunts]

1208
01:14:51,559 --> 01:14:52,727
[grunts]

1209
01:14:55,263 --> 01:14:58,299
[tense music]

1210
01:15:06,607 --> 01:15:08,476
[knife clatters]

1211
01:15:10,812 --> 01:15:13,547
- [gunshots]
- [panting]

1212
01:15:15,950 --> 01:15:17,385
[gun clicks]

1213
01:15:26,895 --> 01:15:28,162
[door groans]

1214
01:15:31,766 --> 01:15:34,168
[tense music intensifies]

1215
01:15:34,969 --> 01:15:35,937
[gunshots]

1216
01:15:42,610 --> 01:15:44,012
[gunshots]

1217
01:15:45,413 --> 01:15:47,081
[gun clicks]

1218
01:15:48,817 --> 01:15:52,721
[both grunting]

1219
01:15:52,821 --> 01:15:54,322
[yells, grunts]

1220
01:15:54,422 --> 01:15:55,824
[Cole exhales sharply]

1221
01:15:55,924 --> 01:15:59,260
[both grunting, straining]

1222
01:15:59,360 --> 01:16:01,662
- [kick lands]
- [grunting]

1223
01:16:01,763 --> 01:16:04,866
- [both grunting]
- [Marko] Ah!

1224
01:16:06,134 --> 01:16:08,937
[Cole yells, grunting in pain]

1225
01:16:09,037 --> 01:16:10,671
- [Marko grunts]
- [Cole yells]

1226
01:16:12,774 --> 01:16:15,209
[Cole straining]

1227
01:16:19,013 --> 01:16:20,381
[grunts]

1228
01:16:20,481 --> 01:16:23,151
[foreboding music]

1229
01:16:33,027 --> 01:16:34,028
[grunts]

1230
01:16:37,565 --> 01:16:39,968
[Marko] Ahh! [grunts]

1231
01:16:40,568 --> 01:16:43,571
[metal groaning]

1232
01:16:47,408 --> 01:16:48,376
[grunts]

1233
01:16:49,643 --> 01:16:52,280
[grunting]

1234
01:16:52,380 --> 01:16:56,117
[grunting continues]

1235
01:16:56,217 --> 01:16:58,987
[yelling, grunting]

1236
01:16:59,087 --> 01:17:00,421
[Marko] Ahh!

1237
01:17:00,521 --> 01:17:03,391
[loud clanging]

1238
01:17:06,727 --> 01:17:08,096
[Marko grunts]

1239
01:17:14,168 --> 01:17:16,838
[straining]

1240
01:17:20,374 --> 01:17:23,411
- [grunts]
- [Marko yelling in pain]

1241
01:17:25,279 --> 01:17:28,282
- [Cole yells]
- [Marko grunts, groans]

1242
01:17:28,382 --> 01:17:31,652
[Cole grunts, coughs]

1243
01:17:31,752 --> 01:17:36,124
[breathing heavily, grunts]

1244
01:17:36,224 --> 01:17:37,926
[Marko grunts]

1245
01:17:42,897 --> 01:17:44,065
[growls]

1246
01:17:48,970 --> 01:17:50,872
You should have died in Bangkok.

1247
01:17:51,605 --> 01:17:53,174
- [hook pierces flesh]
- [Marko yells in pain]

1248
01:17:53,274 --> 01:17:55,476
[both grunting]

1249
01:17:55,576 --> 01:17:57,645
[Marko yells, grunts in pain]

1250
01:17:57,745 --> 01:18:00,448
- [Cole grunting]
- [Marko grunts, yells in pain]

1251
01:18:00,548 --> 01:18:05,619
Aah! [panting, grunting]

1252
01:18:07,255 --> 01:18:09,757
- [Marko growls] Aah!
- [grunts]

1253
01:18:09,858 --> 01:18:12,193
- [grunts]
- [yelling in pain]

1254
01:18:12,293 --> 01:18:14,896
[Marko grunting in pain]

1255
01:18:18,166 --> 01:18:19,133
[grunts in pain]

1256
01:18:20,001 --> 01:18:22,736
[yelling in pain]

1257
01:18:23,571 --> 01:18:24,906
Ah!

1258
01:18:25,006 --> 01:18:26,440
This is for Tibu.

1259
01:18:38,752 --> 01:18:39,820
[spear gun thuds]

1260
01:18:45,927 --> 01:18:46,928
[sighs]

1261
01:18:47,028 --> 01:18:49,497
[dramatic music]

1262
01:18:56,204 --> 01:18:59,173
[bird squawking]

1263
01:19:04,445 --> 01:19:07,348
[bird continues squawking]

1264
01:19:17,391 --> 01:19:20,294
[dramatic music continues]

1265
01:19:29,537 --> 01:19:31,139
[Tully] Stay the fuck down.

1266
01:19:34,642 --> 01:19:36,010
Just stay down.

1267
01:19:37,545 --> 01:19:40,481
Don't you fucking move.

1268
01:19:40,581 --> 01:19:42,416
- Get the cuffs on him.
- [Navy Seal] Yes, sir.

1269
01:19:46,554 --> 01:19:47,721
[Angie] Wait!

1270
01:19:49,690 --> 01:19:50,658
[Navy Seal] Move it.

1271
01:19:50,758 --> 01:19:52,793
[running footsteps]

1272
01:19:52,893 --> 01:19:53,861
[Angie grunts]

1273
01:20:00,168 --> 01:20:01,302
[Angie] I'm not armed.

1274
01:20:02,003 --> 01:20:04,305
- Who are you?
- I'm Angie Ellis. I called you.

1275
01:20:04,405 --> 01:20:05,839
I'm the third mate.

1276
01:20:06,941 --> 01:20:08,276
He has nothing to do with this.

1277
01:20:08,842 --> 01:20:10,244
He saved us.

1278
01:20:10,344 --> 01:20:11,745
[Tully] Where's the rest
of the crew?

1279
01:20:13,114 --> 01:20:14,115
[Angie] They're dead.

1280
01:20:14,215 --> 01:20:16,084
[Tully] How many were there?

1281
01:20:16,184 --> 01:20:19,353
[Angie] About 20.
And the captain.

1282
01:20:21,889 --> 01:20:23,091
Is that Cole Reed?

1283
01:20:23,191 --> 01:20:24,358
No.

1284
01:20:25,226 --> 01:20:26,360
That's my shipmate.

1285
01:20:29,930 --> 01:20:33,434
You're telling us
that that isn't Cole?

1286
01:20:34,368 --> 01:20:36,637
Cole was shot.
He went overboard.

1287
01:20:38,039 --> 01:20:39,073
Ah.

1288
01:20:41,275 --> 01:20:43,644
- So that's how it went down?
- [inhales]

1289
01:20:43,744 --> 01:20:47,281
Yeah, that's how
it went down, sir.

1290
01:20:50,251 --> 01:20:51,752
[Tully] Keep an eye on her.

1291
01:20:53,321 --> 01:20:54,288
[exhales]

1292
01:20:55,756 --> 01:20:56,824
[Tully] Get him up.

1293
01:20:59,493 --> 01:21:01,262
Looks like you had a rough day.

1294
01:21:02,997 --> 01:21:04,232
Let's check you out.

1295
01:21:05,133 --> 01:21:07,801
There are people on that ship
that need medical attention.

1296
01:21:11,839 --> 01:21:13,974
- All right?
- Oh, yeah.

1297
01:21:16,677 --> 01:21:18,279
[Angie] Yes, that's correct.

1298
01:21:19,413 --> 01:21:21,615
I'll be waiting. Thank you.

1299
01:21:25,319 --> 01:21:26,654
They're sending me a crew
to help me

1300
01:21:26,754 --> 01:21:28,156
with the route back to LA.

1301
01:21:29,290 --> 01:21:31,025
[smacks lips]
So it's Captain Ellis now.

1302
01:21:31,125 --> 01:21:32,093
[laughs]

1303
01:21:32,193 --> 01:21:33,561
[Seng speaks Thai]

1304
01:21:33,661 --> 01:21:35,463
[Angie in English]
Yeah, I don't think so.

1305
01:21:36,497 --> 01:21:38,566
Is that Captain Marko's
sat phone?

1306
01:21:38,666 --> 01:21:40,368
It is.

1307
01:21:40,468 --> 01:21:41,902
Does it have a call log on it?

1308
01:21:42,002 --> 01:21:43,104
Of course.

1309
01:21:46,974 --> 01:21:48,709
- [Angie chuckles]
- Thank you.

1310
01:21:52,380 --> 01:21:53,447
Thank you.

1311
01:21:57,451 --> 01:22:00,521
[indistinct chatter]

1312
01:22:02,123 --> 01:22:03,524
[Angie]
So, where will you go now?

1313
01:22:04,358 --> 01:22:06,060
If you go back to Bangkok,

1314
01:22:06,160 --> 01:22:08,028
you know that they're gonna try
and kill you.

1315
01:22:09,730 --> 01:22:11,165
I need to finish this.

1316
01:22:15,803 --> 01:22:17,071
Get home to Violet.

1317
01:22:19,407 --> 01:22:20,974
[chuckles softly] I will.

1318
01:22:24,678 --> 01:22:26,314
[gasps softly] Ah.

1319
01:22:26,414 --> 01:22:29,683
[soft music]

1320
01:22:38,526 --> 01:22:40,128
[Spencer]
Is the Artemis secured?

1321
01:22:40,694 --> 01:22:42,696
[Tully]
Yes, sir.
Artemis secure.

1322
01:22:43,264 --> 01:22:45,266
[Spencer]
Is Cole Reed secured?

1323
01:22:45,866 --> 01:22:49,069
According to Miss Ellis,
Reed was killed in action, sir.

1324
01:22:49,703 --> 01:22:52,340
Marko and all 20
of his crew killed.

1325
01:22:52,440 --> 01:22:54,074
Twenty killed?

1326
01:22:54,175 --> 01:22:55,343
[Tully over sat phone]
Twenty-one, sir.

1327
01:22:55,443 --> 01:22:56,510
Plus the pirates.

1328
01:22:57,745 --> 01:23:01,014
There was one friendly crewman
we didn't identify

1329
01:23:01,115 --> 01:23:04,852
who appears to be taking off
on the pirate boat, sir.

1330
01:23:06,920 --> 01:23:08,722
[Spencer]
Wait a second.
Let me get this straight.

1331
01:23:09,357 --> 01:23:12,293
Cole Reed is KIA,
but you do not have a body,

1332
01:23:12,393 --> 01:23:14,595
and now, there's
this unidentified crewman

1333
01:23:14,695 --> 01:23:17,097
heading off on a pirate ship.

1334
01:23:17,198 --> 01:23:18,699
Do I have that correct?

1335
01:23:19,800 --> 01:23:21,402
[Tully]
Yes, sir, that's correct.

1336
01:23:23,036 --> 01:23:24,638
You want us to intercept?

1337
01:23:26,240 --> 01:23:29,910
Well, since he is not Cole Reed,
he is not our problem.

1338
01:23:31,645 --> 01:23:33,281
I would agree, sir.

1339
01:23:33,381 --> 01:23:36,617
[tense music]

1340
01:23:37,285 --> 01:23:41,555
[cell phone ringing]

1341
01:23:44,124 --> 01:23:45,193
[Cole over phone]
It's me.

1342
01:23:45,293 --> 01:23:46,394
Jesus. Where are you?

1343
01:23:46,927 --> 01:23:48,629
I need you to run a number.

1344
01:23:48,729 --> 01:23:49,763
One sec.

1345
01:23:54,402 --> 01:23:55,503
- [keyboard clacks]
- Go on.

1346
01:23:55,603 --> 01:24:00,007
667-213-4777.

1347
01:24:02,243 --> 01:24:03,811
[Taran] Jaran Daniles.

1348
01:24:04,945 --> 01:24:06,013
I'm coming back.

1349
01:24:06,880 --> 01:24:07,948
[sat phone beeps]

1350
01:24:08,682 --> 01:24:11,519
[tense music continues]

1351
01:24:21,094 --> 01:24:22,896
[woman] Such a lovely service.

1352
01:24:22,996 --> 01:24:25,666
I thought everyone did
such a beautiful job.

1353
01:24:25,766 --> 01:24:28,369
[man] The community
will miss him so much.

1354
01:24:30,471 --> 01:24:33,374
[foreboding music]

1355
01:24:36,977 --> 01:24:37,945
Get in.

1356
01:24:41,449 --> 01:24:42,450
[car door closes]

1357
01:24:49,557 --> 01:24:52,293
[Cole breathes deeply]

1358
01:24:55,529 --> 01:24:56,697
You don't understand.

1359
01:24:58,799 --> 01:25:01,068
I just let them use the ships
to transport cargo,

1360
01:25:01,168 --> 01:25:02,370
and they paid me.

1361
01:25:03,237 --> 01:25:04,505
They paid me a lot.

1362
01:25:06,674 --> 01:25:10,311
But I had no idea what they were
really asking me to do.

1363
01:25:10,411 --> 01:25:11,879
You have to believe me.

1364
01:25:13,981 --> 01:25:16,750
And then they stopped asking
and they started threatening.

1365
01:25:17,885 --> 01:25:19,587
And that's when things
got out of hand.

1366
01:25:21,355 --> 01:25:23,824
Multiple shipments every week.

1367
01:25:26,327 --> 01:25:28,061
Why didn't you come to me?

1368
01:25:28,161 --> 01:25:30,431
Because I thought
I had it handled.

1369
01:25:33,434 --> 01:25:35,703
I thought selling the company
would get me out.

1370
01:25:38,205 --> 01:25:40,308
But I never knew that they...

1371
01:25:40,874 --> 01:25:42,543
I didn't think
they'd go this far.

1372
01:25:45,245 --> 01:25:46,847
You got your father killed.

1373
01:25:46,947 --> 01:25:49,216
[sighs, inhales sharply]

1374
01:25:51,619 --> 01:25:53,220
And you're gonna have to live
with that.

1375
01:25:54,522 --> 01:25:55,923
For the rest of your life.

1376
01:25:58,091 --> 01:25:59,593
[inhales shakily]

1377
01:26:04,698 --> 01:26:06,867
[sighs] Take him home.

1378
01:26:06,967 --> 01:26:08,436
[car door opens]

1379
01:26:10,304 --> 01:26:11,271
[car door closes]

1380
01:26:12,272 --> 01:26:15,309
[intense music]

1381
01:26:39,967 --> 01:26:41,602
[loud crash]

1382
01:26:46,340 --> 01:26:48,642
[metal squeaking]

1383
01:26:51,745 --> 01:26:53,747
[engine hisses]

1384
01:26:56,784 --> 01:26:57,951
[car door closes]

1385
01:26:59,787 --> 01:27:01,121
[Daniles groaning]

1386
01:27:06,427 --> 01:27:07,628
[Daniles gasps]

1387
01:27:09,797 --> 01:27:15,268
[grunting, panting]

1388
01:27:16,637 --> 01:27:18,005
Why kill Tibu?

1389
01:27:19,473 --> 01:27:22,242
Tibu dies,
the company goes to Kameron,

1390
01:27:22,342 --> 01:27:25,112
who's compromised,
who we control,

1391
01:27:25,212 --> 01:27:26,880
and our cargo business goes on.

1392
01:27:26,980 --> 01:27:29,216
You mean the human beings
you were trafficking?

1393
01:27:30,350 --> 01:27:33,020
What do you want?
[continues panting]

1394
01:27:33,120 --> 01:27:34,955
Everybody wants something.

1395
01:27:35,055 --> 01:27:37,958
Tell me what you want.
I'll get it for you.

1396
01:27:40,628 --> 01:27:42,295
What the fuck do you want?

1397
01:27:42,963 --> 01:27:44,798
[Daniles grunts]

1398
01:27:52,372 --> 01:27:53,574
Vengeance.

1399
01:27:54,241 --> 01:27:57,310
[intense music]

1400
01:29:34,307 --> 01:29:35,576
[music fades out]

1401
01:29:35,676 --> 01:29:38,345
[tense music]

1402
01:30:47,581 --> 01:30:49,049
[music fades out]

1403
01:30:49,149 --> 01:30:52,185
[unsettling music]

1404
01:31:50,778 --> 01:31:51,812
[music fades out]

1405
01:31:51,912 --> 01:31:54,948
[intriguing music]

1406
01:32:55,308 --> 01:32:57,144
[music fades out]

1407
01:32:59,212 --> 01:33:02,282
[soft music]

1408
01:33:59,106 --> 01:34:00,140
[music fades out]

1409
01:34:00,240 --> 01:34:03,276
[dramatic music]

1410
01:34:54,928 --> 01:34:56,830
[music fades out]

